    ('cow:COW', 'https://docs.google.com/document/d/18dHk-J2-hhmTrp2Z4sieNycI1tZpW3wWUuVAQXddxfI/edit', $tank_seed_COW_20261110$## COW — CoW Protocol: token & protocol fact sheet

As of 2026-11-10

Scope and naming: "CoW Protocol" is the intent-based trading/settlement protocol; "CoW Swap" is its main front-end (swap.cow.fi); "CoW DAO" is the token-holder governance body that owns the products; "CoW AMM" is its LP product; "MEV Blocker" is a MEV-protection RPC that CoW DAO co-created and sold to Consensys' Special Mechanisms Group in January 2026. The COW token governs all of these. On-chain reads below were taken at Ethereum block 26,385,217 (2026-11-10 14:50 UTC) unless stated otherwise. Market data: CoinGecko, 2026-11-10 15:52 UTC (fact-check refresh).

### 1. Executive summary

COW is the governance token of CoW DAO, the owner of CoW Protocol, an intent-based DEX aggregator. Users sign orders, and bonded third-party "solvers" compete in batch auctions to settle them. The protocol is a real, fee-earning business: DefiLlama shows $19.37M of protocol revenue over the trailing 365 days and $1.30M over the last 30 days (about $15–16M annualized). CoW's own figure of about $41.9M cumulative revenue from 2024 to mid-May 2026 matches DefiLlama's $41.5M for the same period. Nothing is distributed to COW holders today. DefiLlama records holder revenue as $0, and the DAO's own Blockworks filing says there are no distributions. Revenue funds open-market COW buybacks (64.4M COW, about $11.6M, over the last 365 days by my on-chain count), but the bought tokens pay solver rewards. They are not burned. Current state: the business is shrinking. Monthly volume fell from about $12.0B (Oct 2025) to about $3.3B (Oct 2026) and monthly revenue from about $2.2M to about $1.3M. COW trades at $0.1027, down 52% in a year, with a $59.0M market cap and a $102.7M FDV (CoinGecko, 2026-11-10 15:52 UTC). The most important thing to watch is whether CoW DAO adopts a real value-distribution mechanism. A burn trial and a flexible buyback mandate were proposed in May 2026 but have not yet gone to a vote; on 2026-09-10 the Core Team said the CIP is "in the roadmap for a Q4 initiative". A related item is buyback execution: no buyback fills have been observed since 2026-10-21, and CIP-92, which ends 2026-11-11, moves buyback duty to the CoW Foundation.

### 2. What the token is

- Ticker: COW (CoW Protocol Token). Native issuance on Ethereum. Type: ERC-20 governance token. There is no staking, no ve-lock and no fee claim.

- TGE: 2022-02-11. 1,000,000,000 COW were minted to the CoW DAO ([Blockworks Token Transparency filing](https://blockworks.com/token-transparency/filing/cow-protocol)).

- Inflation option: the contract lets governance mint up to 3% of total supply, at most once every 365 days ([docs.cow.fi/governance/token](https://docs.cow.fi/governance/token)). It has never been used: on-chain totalSupply() = 1,000,000,000.0 COW on 2026-11-10.

