### 3. How it works

#### The product for users

- Intents, not transactions. A user signs an off-chain order (EIP-712 or EIP-1271) that states the sell and buy tokens, amounts, limit price and expiry. Orders that cannot settle cost the user no gas. Settlement gas is paid by solvers and recovered inside the execution price ("gasless" trading).

- Batch auctions. Orders are grouped into batches. Since CIP-67 (May 2025) the protocol uses a "Fair Combinatorial Auction": bonded solvers bid on individual orders or groups of orders. The protocol's off-chain "autopilot" picks the winners by user surplus, and the winning solver submits the settlement to GPv2Settlement (0x9008D19f58AAbD9eD0D60971565AA8510560ab41 on Ethereum). That contract checks that every fill is at or above the user's signed limit price. Verity formally verified this property of settle() in October 2026.

- Coincidence of Wants (CoW). When two users want opposite sides of a pair in the same batch, a solver can match them directly, with no AMM fee and no exposure to MEV. Other fills route through AMMs, other aggregators or private market makers.

- MEV protection. Orders never sit in the public mempool as swaps, and a batch clears at uniform prices, so sandwich attacks are structurally hard. This is the core user pitch. It is not a guarantee: the March 2026 incident involved a settlement transaction leaking to the public mempool.

- Order types: market swaps, limit orders, TWAP (opened to normal wallets in September 2026; previously Safe-only), programmatic/conditional orders, flash-loan-backed "Atomic Bundles" (May 2026) and cross-chain swaps (via bridge providers and NEAR Intents, including BTC since July 2026).

- Chains: Ethereum, Gnosis, Arbitrum, Base, Polygon, Avalanche, BNB, Lens, Linea, Plasma and Ink, with Solana in progress (docs; recaps).

#### Solvers

- Solvers are allow-listed through GPv2AllowListAuthentication, an upgradeable proxy. Solvers are added and removed by the "Solver Controller" Safe 0x423cEc87f19F0778f549846e0801ee267a917935 (on-chain getThreshold/getOwners on 2026-11-10: 4-of-13; the Blockworks filing states 4/15); the proxy owner is the DAO Safe. A solver must post a bond: a full bond, or a reduced bond via the CoW DAO bonding pool. The Core Team counts 5 full bonds (7.5M COW) and 5 reduced bonds (2.5M COW) (forum 3454). A June 2026 draft proposes a reduced bond of $200k in stables/ETH, or $100k plus 0.5M COW.

- Solvers are paid weekly from the Solver Payouts Safe. Since CIP-74 (passed 2025-11-13), the second-price reward is capped dynamically by the protocol fees that the winning solution generates. CIP-85 (2026-04-06) added performance and consistency rewards, capped at 50% of protocol revenue. CIP-88 (2026-09-25) created a quote-competition reward budget of about 10% of protocol revenue. CIP-87 (2026-08-25) changed solver penalties to a percentage of trade size.

#### Governance mechanics

- Off-chain voting on Snapshot (space cow.eth). Voting power is the balance of COW plus vCOW on Ethereum and Gnosis Chain, including delegations (Snapshot space strategies), and quorum is 35,000,000 COW. Approved CIPs are executed by the 3-of-5 DAO Safe (on-chain read: threshold 3, owners 5).

- Legal wrapper (CIP-64, March 2025): CoW Foundation (Cayman foundation company) owns the IP and acts as the DAO's legal interface. It has three BVI subsidiaries: CoW Core Ltd (development), CoW Hosting Ltd (front-end, domains) and CoW Business Ltd (solver payouts, buyback execution, partner and CEX relations). Staff are contracted through Nomev Labs, Lda ("Lda" is a Portuguese company form; named Service Provider since CIP-58) under annual service agreements: CIP-79 for 2026 at $12.6M; CIP-91 for 2027 at $10.45M is being voted on.

- GPv2Settlement is non-upgradeable and non-pausable. Neither the Foundation nor CoW Core holds pause or upgrade keys over it or over the token (Blockworks filing). In practice, control sits with the DAO Safe and the solver allow-list Safe, and the auction itself runs on core-team infrastructure.

#### Token mechanics, plainly

| Mechanism | Exists? | Detail |

| --- | --- | --- |

| Governance | Yes | Snapshot votes on fees, solver rules, treasury, budgets. |

| Staking / ve-lock | No | "Locked-token rights: NA" (Blockworks filing). |

| Fee switch to holders | No | "There are currently no dividends ... or distributions of profit" (Blockworks filing). DefiLlama holder revenue = $0. |

| Buyback | Yes (CIP-36, CIP-38, CIP-48) | Protocol fees, converted to WETH, are TWAP-sold for COW on CoW Swap. The target is weekly solver emissions plus 20%. The bought COW is used to pay solvers and is not burned. |

| Burn | No | A 1:1 burn trial through December 2026 (est. 60–85M COW) was proposed on 2026-05-15 but has not been put to a vote as of 2026-11-10 (Core Team, 2026-09-10: "in the roadmap for a Q4 initiative"). |

| Gas / collateral | No | COW is not used as gas. Since October 2026 it can pay for x402 API quotes on Base. It is accepted as collateral on Binance margin (ratio raised from 10% to 30% on 2026-10-23 per [CryptoTicker](https://cryptoticker.io/en/binance-shiba-inu-collateral-60-percent-october-2026/)). |

| Solver bonds | Partially | Bonds can be posted partly in COW (e.g. $100k + 0.5M COW under the draft rules). |

### 4. Utility

- Real utility today:

- governance over a fee-generating protocol and a KPK-managed treasury of about $26.5M (mostly stablecoins and ETH, plus a small COW position; 2026-06-30) and 357M COW in the DAO Safe;

- the unit of account for solver rewards (solvers receive COW and are expected to keep part of it as alignment and bond capital);

- partial solver-bond collateral;

- since October 2026, an optional payment asset for x402.cow.fi quotes on Base at $0.001 per quote.

- Not needed for:

- trading on CoW Swap (fees are taken in the traded tokens);

- gas;

- LP-ing in CoW AMM;

- integrating the API or widget;

- receiving any share of fees.

- Conclusion: COW is effectively a governance token with an indirect, discretionary link to revenue. The DAO buys COW with revenue, but only to cover its own solver incentive costs. The Core Team itself states that "protocol growth alone doesn't create structural token demand" ([May 2026 recap](https://cow.fi/learn/cow-dao-monthly-recap-may-2026)). It has said a dividend-like mechanism could make COW a security, and it framed $10M of free cash flow as the "hurdle point" for automatic value distribution (forum 3454, 2026-06-18).

### 5. Why people buy and sell it

#### Demand drivers

- Valuation vs fundamentals:

- Market cap $59.0M against $19.4M trailing-365d revenue gives about 3.0x market cap/revenue and about 5.3x FDV/revenue (2026-11-10). Forum holders argue the token is "disconnected from fundamentals".

- Peer comparison (CoinGecko, 2026-11-10): 1INCH has a $105M market cap; ZRX (0x) has $74M.

- Buyback flow: COW is continuously bought with revenue. Over the last 365 days that was about 64.4M COW, roughly $11.6M. Holders treat this as structural bid support, although the tokens re-enter circulation as solver rewards.

- Tokenomics catalyst: the pending "Path to Value Distribution". It proposes a burn trial and a mandate to scale buybacks up to 100% of weekly revenue (forum 3454).

- Narratives:

- intents and solver networks;

- MEV protection;

- CoW as the execution layer embedded in other products: MetaMask Agent Wallet, MetaMask Swaps, Lido, Aave, Euler, Jumper, Bitget Wallet, Gate Web3, Ambire;

- AI-agent trading (x402);

- tokenized stocks (xStocks, cbMEGA);

- Solana expansion.

- Exchange access: listed on Binance, Upbit and Bithumb (Korean exchange integrations were noted in the [2025 review](https://cow.fi/learn/cow-dao-2025-in-review)) and many smaller CEXs.

#### Supply and sell pressure

- Solver rewards: 54.2M COW left the Solver Payouts Safe in 365 days and 13.1M in the last 90 days. Solvers are businesses, and many sell. Only a soft "HODL 25%" rule exists, and the Core Team proposed enforcing 20% via bond Safes.

- Team grant stream (CIP-83) and grants. Up to 100M COW more is possible under the performance tier.

- 121.7M swappable vCOW held by early insiders, investors and GnosisDAO.

- Thin liquidity: about $1.4M of 24h trading volume (CoinGecko, 2026-11-10), so modest sales move price.

- Fundamental drift: declining volume, revenue and aggregator share through 2026, and the March and April 2026 incidents.

- Recent buyback pause: no TWAP fills have been observed since 2026-10-21 (section 8).

### 6. The protocol/business

#### What it does

CoW DAO runs an intent-based trading stack with these product lines:

- CoW Protocol: the settlement and solver-auction layer, sold B2B through API, SDK, widget and Atomic Bundles.

- CoW Swap: the retail and pro front-end, with swaps, limits, TWAP and cross-chain swaps.

- CoW AMM: an LP-protecting AMM launched on Balancer. It is now marginal: DefiLlama shows $38k TVL for "Balancer CoW AMM", and Balancer DAO is voting on its own wind-down (CIP-89 text).

- MEV Blocker: a 50% stake, sold to SMG/Consensys in January 2026 under CIP-73. Sale proceeds are paid in quarterly installments through October 2028 according to DefiLlama's adapter. CoW reports the RPC served more than 4.5M unique users and returned 6,177 ETH in rebates ([CoW blog, 2026-01-26](https://cow.fi/learn/special-mechanisms-group-acquires-mev-blocker-rpc-to-advance-state-of-the-art-backrunning-auction-infrastructure)). The sale price was not disclosed.

#### Audience

- Ethereum-mainnet DeFi traders who care about MEV and price quality, especially large orders, Safe multisig users, DAO treasuries and whales (TWAP).

- Integrators that embed CoW execution: wallets, lending and staking UIs, and treasury tools such as Lido NEST's automated LDO buybacks.

- Growing retail flow on BNB Chain and Base.

- October 2026 user base: 144.6k active wallets (103.8k new, 40.8k returning) and 586,828 trades ([Oct 2026 recap](https://cow.fi/learn/co-w-dao-monthly-recap-october-2026)).

#### Where it is popular

Volume is overwhelmingly on Ethereum mainnet. DefiLlama 30-day volume to 2026-11-09:

- Ethereum: $3.12B of $3.44B (about 91%)

- Base: $136M

- Arbitrum: $106M

- BNB: $51M

- Polygon: $11M

- Avalanche: $8M

- Gnosis: $7M

CoW's own October figures are similar: Ethereum $2.9B, Base $137.2M, Arbitrum $104.5M, BNB $64.6M, Polygon $13.9M. The UI was localized into PT-BR, ES, FR and RU in October 2026. The token has a Korean exchange presence (Upbit and Bithumb). There is no hard data on users by region.

