### 7. Revenue and value capture

#### Fee mechanism (current, per [docs.cow.fi/governance/fees](https://docs.cow.fi/governance/fees))

- Quote-improvement fee: 50% of positive improvement over the quote on market orders, capped at 0.98% of volume.

- Surplus fee: 50% of surplus on out-of-market limit orders and discrete TWAP orders, capped at 0.98%.

- Volume fee: 2 bps on standard pairs and 0.3 bps on correlated pairs (stables and RWAs). Introduced under CIP-74 (2025-11-13); tiered from 2026-02-03. Solana is proposed at 0 bps for 12 months.

- Partner fees: set by the integrator. The default split is 75% to the partner and 25% to the DAO (CIP-75, November 2025; previously 50/50).

- Fee-setting authority: CIP-90 (passed 2026-10-28) gives the core team a standing mandate to set fees within these bounds:

- volume fee between −0.5% and +0.5%;

- at least 50% of price-improvement fees go to the DAO;

- fees "must never go to core team members ... without first entering the CoW DAO treasury".

How fees are collected:

- Fees are not separate transfers. They are embedded in execution, in the surplus token.

- Solvers keep them inside the settlement, and weekly accounting charges solvers for them in the chain's native token.

- Collected fees end up in the Solver Payouts Safe 0xA03be496e67Ec29bC62F01a428683D7F9c204930, which "receives collected fees from the settlement contract" ([docs multisigs](https://docs.cow.fi/governance/multisigs)).

- The Solver Controller Safe converts them to ETH.

#### (a) Gross fees, (b) protocol revenue, (c) holder value

| Period (to 2026-11-09 UTC) | (a) Fees paid by users | (b) Revenue to CoW DAO | (c) To COW holders | COW bought back (on-chain) |

| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |

| 24h (2026-11-09) | $82,505 | $51,871 | $0 | 0 COW |

| 7d | $505,507 | $314,887 | $0 | 0 COW |

| 30d | $2,038,934 | $1,299,235 | $0 | 2.13M COW (≈$0.29M) |

| 90d | $5,903,506 | $3,701,702 | $0 | 11.81M COW (≈$1.58M) |

| 365d | $30,030,549 | $19,370,762 | $0 | 64.37M COW (≈$11.62M) |

| Annualized from 30d (estimate) | ≈$24.8M | ≈$15.8M | $0 | n/a |

| All-time (DefiLlama) | $72.35M | $48.66M | $0 | n/a |

Sources and notes:

- Fee and revenue figures are from the DefiLlama API (/summary/fees/cowswap, pulled 2026-11-10). Buyback amounts are COW transferred from GPv2Settlement to the Buyback Recipient Safe (Etherscan V2). USD values use CoinGecko daily prices.

- DefiLlama "revenue" counts protocol fees, the DAO's 25% of partner fees, 50% of MEV Blocker fees and 50% of MEV Blocker sale installments.

- DefiLlama's chart has a one-off spike on 2025-11-04: $7.40M fees and $3.82M revenue in a single day. Its cause is not documented. The spike is almost entirely on Ethereum ($7.36M fees / $3.79M revenue), and revenue is ~51% of fees that day, consistent with a 50/50-split item (MEV Blocker fees or sale proceeds per the adapter), but this is an inference. It falls outside every window in the table.

- Monthly revenue (DefiLlama): Oct 2025 $2.21M; Nov $5.85M (including the spike); Dec $2.33M; Jan 2026 $2.29M; Feb $2.73M; Mar $1.61M; Apr $1.41M; May $1.01M; Jun $1.76M; Jul $0.84M; Aug $1.09M; Sep $1.21M; Oct $1.29M.

- Chain split of 30d revenue: Ethereum $1.166M (90%), Base $50k, BSC $42k, Arbitrum $31k.

Cross-check. The Core Team states that the DAO has generated $41.9M of revenue since 2024 (forum 3454, 2026-05-15), and the May 2026 recap gives an all-time figure of $42M. DefiLlama's cumulative revenue to 2026-05-15 is $41.54M. The two independent sources agree within 1%.

Where the money goes (on-chain, Ethereum):

- Fee collection. Fee tokens are converted into WETH that lands in the Solver Payouts Safe. 207.7 WETH arrived from GPv2Settlement in 784 transfers over the last 30 days.

- Funding the buyback. The Payouts Safe sends WETH to a buyback-executor Safe, 0x22af3D38E50ddedeb7C47f36faB321eC3Bb72A76 (2-of-5): 264.5 WETH in October and 185.5 WETH in early November 2026.

- Buying COW. The executor places CoW Swap TWAP orders that sell 4.428571 WETH per 12-hour part for COW, with the receiver set to the Buyback Recipient Safe 0xA2BFc70e63a48BDfc3F8013a44B04b6c33fb8200.

- Paying solvers. The Buyback Recipient tops up the Payouts Safe: 7,500,000 COW on 2026-11-04, and 17.5M COW over 90 days. The Payouts Safe then pays solvers in COW and reimburses network costs in ETH (about 357 ETH sent out in 30 days).

- Surplus WETH goes to the Treasury (e.g. 120.62 WETH on 2026-11-04).

Net emissions. The official mandate (CIP-38) is to buy back weekly solver emissions plus 20%. Execution moved from the Treasury team to the Core Team in November 2025 (forum 3454); CIP-92 would move the responsibility to the CoW Foundation and states "No new buyback programme is authorised". Reported results:

- Core Team, as of 2026-05-08: 78,616,859 COW bought back against 66,588,732 COW of solver emissions since 2024-04-17, a net of −12,028,127 COW.

- 2025: 37.6M COW bought against 32.9M emitted.

- Q1 2026 (CoW's figure): 2,822,135 bought against 3,420,726 rewarded.

My on-chain count does not match CoW's Q1 figure: 22.79M COW arrived in the Buyback Recipient Safe from settlements in January–March 2026 (3.87M, 13.27M and 5.65M). CoW's quarterly reporting methodology is not documented. Over the last 90 days the balance has turned: 11.81M COW bought against 13.08M COW sent out of the Payouts Safe.

Does value reach holders? Not directly. Buybacks absorb sell pressure created by the DAO's own solver incentive payments. They neutralize dilution from solver emissions, but they are an operating cost, not a distribution. Bought COW is held in DAO-controlled Safes (24.3M in Buyback Recipient, 7.4M in Payouts) and is not burned. DefiLlama states "No revenue to COW token holders".

Profitability. Two cost lines stand against revenue of $19.4M (trailing 365 days):

- COW purchases for solver rewards: about $11.6M over the same period.

- Core service budget (CIP-79): $12.6M for 2026, of which $10.85M had been invoiced by 2026-10-28.

On these numbers, revenue alone does not cover both. The Core Team nonetheless describes the last 2–3 quarters as "moving to profitability", and the definitions are not reconciled publicly. The Core Team sets a $10M free-cash-flow hurdle before value distribution kicks in. The treasury fell from $34.36M to $26.54M in H1 2026 (KPK), mostly because of operational transfers: CIP-79 USDC, CIP-83 COW and CIP-86 reimbursements.

Stated plan to deliver value ("CoW DAO's Path to Value Distribution", [forum 3454](https://forum.cow.fi/t/cow-daos-path-to-value-distribution-core-team-view/3454), 2026-05-15, prepared with Aragon under the Value Distribution RFP):

- Enforce a solver "HODL rule": 20% of rewards go to Solver Bond Safes.

- A 1:1 burn trial through December 2026, estimated to remove 60–85M COW.

- A flexible buyback mandate of up to 100% of weekly revenue.

A revised circulating-supply definition was also proposed. Aragon (leuts.eth) recommended a single, traceable buy-and-burn address. As of 2026-11-10, no corresponding CIP has been put to a Snapshot vote (Snapshot cow.eth list). On 2026-09-10 the Core Team (notsoformal) wrote that it is "in the roadmap for a Q4 initiative" and that attention had been diverted to protocol-level work.

### 8. How to verify on-chain

All values below were obtained on 2026-11-10 between about 14:45 and 15:30 UTC. Replace $ETHERSCAN_API_KEY with your own key. Never commit keys.

#### Key addresses (Ethereum)

| Role | Address | What I read |

| --- | --- | --- |

| COW token | 0xDEf1CA1fb7FBcDC777520aa7f396b4E015F497aB | totalSupply 1,000,000,000.0 |

| GPv2Settlement | 0x9008D19f58AAbD9eD0D60971565AA8510560ab41 | Emits Trade events (topic0 0xa07a543ab8a018198e99ca0184c93fe9050a79400a0a723441f84de1d972cc17) |

| CoW DAO main Safe | 0xcA771eda0c70aA7d053aB1B25004559B918FE662 | 357,338,386 COW; 3-of-5. Only one COW outflow in the last 400 days (2,677,125 COW on 2026-04-30). |

| Solver Payouts Safe (fee collector) | 0xA03be496e67Ec29bC62F01a428683D7F9c204930 | 7,365,310 COW; 227.25 WETH; 4-of-12 |

| Solver Controller Safe | 0x423cEc87f19F0778f549846e0801ee267a917935 | 0 COW (manages the allow-list and fee-to-ETH conversion) |

| Buyback executor Safe (TWAP order owner) | 0x22af3D38E50ddedeb7C47f36faB321eC3Bb72A76 | 2-of-5. Last fill 2026-10-21 23:49 UTC (tx 0xed84c38b…6857966: 4.428571 WETH → 79,358.44 COW) |

| CoW Buyback Recipient Safe | 0xA2BFc70e63a48BDfc3F8013a44B04b6c33fb8200 | 24,344,850 COW; 3-of-5 |

