### Verification notes

Independent fact-check performed 2026-11-10, approx. 15:30–16:00 UTC, against primary sources and on-chain reads (Ethereum block ~26,385,530).

#### Re-checked and confirmed

- Supply: COW totalSupply() = 1,000,000,000.0 (publicnode RPC). Bridged contracts on Gnosis, Arbitrum, Base, Polygon and BNB all return symbol COW and match CoinGecko "platforms"; their supplies are 18,195,547 / 875,260 / 910,823 / 6 / 404,521 COW.

- Balances and Safe thresholds (on-chain): DAO Safe 357,338,386 COW, 3-of-5; Buyback Recipient 24,344,850 COW, 3-of-5; Solver Payouts 7,365,310 COW and 227.25 WETH, 4-of-12; buyback executor 2-of-5; CoW Treasury 512,737 COW, 3-of-6; Omni bridge 18,321,894; Binance 20,424,415; top-holder list matches Blockscout.

- DefiLlama (slug cowswap, re-queried): all 24h/7d/30d/90d/365d/all-time fees and revenue match exactly; holders revenue is 0 in every period. Monthly revenue and volume series match. Cumulative revenue from 2024 to 2026-05-15 is $41.54M, against the Core Team's $41.9M. Aggregator ranking (7th, 5.2% of $64.0B 30d volume) matches.

- Methodology: the DefiLlama adapter source confirms that revenue includes 50% of MEV Blocker fees and sale proceeds and the DAO's partner-fee share, and sets HoldersRevenue to 0.

- Buybacks (Etherscan V2, recomputed independently): COW from GPv2Settlement into the Buyback Recipient was 2.13M (30d), 11.81M (90d) and 64.37M (365d). Jan, Feb and Mar 2026 were 3.87M, 13.27M and 5.65M. The last fill was 2026-10-21 23:49 UTC, tx 0xed84…7966, 79,358.44 COW; the CoW API trades endpoint returns the same fill as the latest. The 7.5M COW (2026-11-04) and 10M COW (2026-09-02) top-ups to Payouts and the 1,179,456 COW Treasury transfer (2026-10-22) are confirmed.

- Solver payouts: 30d 5.09M and 90d 13.08M confirmed. For 365d I get 54.09M against the draft's 54.22M (0.2% difference, likely from block-boundary pagination of the Etherscan 10k-row window).

- Market data: CoinGecko was re-read at 15:52 UTC. Price, market cap, FDV, volume and 30d change had moved slightly and were updated. Circulating supply 574,488,169, ATH and 1y change are unchanged.

- Governance (Snapshot GraphQL): the dates and vote totals of CIP-73 through CIP-93 match, including CIP-76 failing (46.57M For vs 57.70M Against) and CIP-90 (39.3M For, 0 Against). Quorum is 35M. CIP-83, CIP-89, CIP-88, CIP-90 and CIP-75 parameters match the proposal texts.

- Forum and official pages:

- Forum 3454: 357.3M COW, vesting end 2026-02-12, 78,616,859 vs 66,588,732, the 60–85M COW burn estimate, the $10M FCF hurdle and the bond counts.

- KPK 3533: $26.54M, $34.36M, $21.98M, $4.57M and 25M COW under CIP-83.

- CIP-91: $10.45M; $10,845,858 invoiced by 2026-10-28.

- CIP-92: $180k→$500k; buyback duty moves to the Foundation.

- CoW recaps for Oct, Jul, Apr, Jan and May 2026 and the 2025 review: the October figures, @fleupold_, Q1 2,822,135/3,420,726, the 60–72M projection, $87B/$40.2B, and the MEV Blocker 4.5M users and 6,177 ETH.

- Blockworks filing: Anna George, Glenn Kennedy, Leeward, the no-distributions statement, the absence of pause/upgrade keys and the incident status.

- docs.cow.fi: fees, allocation, the 3%/365-day mint cap and the multisig roles.

#### Corrected

- Solver Controller Safe is 4-of-13 on-chain, not 4-of-15. The Blockworks figure is retained as a note.

