#### Not independently verified

- The Block articles (March 2026 $50.4M swap with the $110,368 fee; the 2022 $23M raise) returned HTTP 403. CoW's own recaps confirm a March trading incident with a post-mortem, and a DNS hijack with about 1.2M USDC drained over about 4.5 hours, reimbursed under CIP-86. The exact $ figures for the March swap rest on The Block.

- Binance raising the COW collateral ratio from 10% to 30% (effective 2026-10-23 06:00 UTC): single secondary source (CryptoTicker citing Tokenpost, 2026-10-21). Binance's ratio endpoint requires an API key, so this was not confirmed.

- The smg.org memo link did not resolve from this environment. The MEV Blocker sale price remains undisclosed.

- Dune pages (HTTP 403) and the competitor revenue column (Jupiter, KyberSwap, OKX) were not re-queried.

- Anna George's personal X handle and a formal CEO title are not confirmed in official sources. The Blockworks filing lists her as "Co-Founder".

- The cause of the Q1 2026 discrepancy (CoW-reported 2.82M COW bought vs 22.79M on-chain inflows) is still unexplained. Both figures were re-verified as stated.

- Web search was unavailable during this fact-check (search budget exhausted), so claims sourced only from news sites were checked only where a primary page could be fetched directly.
