    ('lighter:LIT', 'https://docs.google.com/document/d/1KQbffBkn-GwK-8wpQkfjWLYJ_ZSeKdjiXazMh99ILqs/edit', $tank_seed_LIT_20261110$## LIT — Lighter: token & protocol fact sheet

As of 2026-11-10

### Executive summary

LIT ("Lighter Infrastructure Token") is the fixed-supply (1,000,000,000) ERC-20 of Lighter, a zk-rollup order-book exchange for perpetual futures (crypto, equities, FX, commodities), spot and, since 19 Oct 2026, binary options. It is run by Elliot Technologies (Delaware) and founder/CEO Vladimir Novakovski. Value does reach holders today. Lighter's treasury buys LIT on its own LIT/USDC order book with fee revenue: $4.29M in the 30 days to 2026-11-09, about $52M annualized. From February to September 2026 buybacks equalled 93–99% of main-exchange (Ethereum-settled) revenue each month; in October and in the latest 30 days they exceeded it (135% and 132%), but they equal only about 80% of combined revenue including Robinhood Chain. Each quarter an amount equal to the quarter's purchases is burned on Ethereum: 18,090,720 LIT are already at the dead address. On-chain, the burned tokens come from the ecosystem reserve, while the repurchased LIT is withdrawn to an operations wallet that recycles it (e.g., for staking rewards), so the net effect is a shrinking reserve rather than destruction of the purchased tokens. I rebuilt these figures trade by trade from the treasury account and they match DefiLlama to the dollar. The business is stable but much smaller than at its peak. Monthly main-exchange volume fell from $292.9B (Nov 2025) to $53.8B (Oct 2026). Robinhood Chain now adds about 25% of combined volume and about 36% of fees. Hyperliquid's 30-day holder revenue is about 16 times Lighter's ($68.2M vs $4.29M). The most important thing to watch is the team and investor unlock. It starts around 27–30 Dec 2026: 500M LIT released linearly over 3 years, about 13.9M LIT per month (about $46M per month at $3.33). That is roughly 11 times the current monthly buyback. The planned CFTC filing in November 2026 is the main bullish catalyst.

### What the token is

- Ticker / name: LIT, ERC-20 named "Lighter" (exchanges such as Coinbase and Kraken list it as "LIGHTER"). Do not confuse it with Litentry (old LIT ticker).

- Ethereum contract (verified): 0x232CE3bD40fCd6f80f3d55A522d03f25Df784Ee2. It is OpenZeppelin ERC20 + ERC20Permit, Solidity 0.8.25, contract name Lighter. The constructor mints MAX_TOTAL_SUPPLY = 1_000_000_000e18 once, to one recipient. There is no mint function after deployment, no burn function, no owner and no proxy (Etherscan source; Proxy=0). Minted 2025-10-27 to deployer 0x077842a5670cb4c83dca62bda4c36592a5b31891 [9].

- Robinhood Chain representation: 0xeeca2e7dc194a320d349122d88259bb9595a4cb0 (CoinGecko platform listing; not independently read on-chain) [12]. Inside the Lighter L2, LIT is asset_id 2 and the LIT/USDC spot market is market_index 2049 [14].

- On-chain supply read (Ethereum block ~26,385,264, 2026-11-10): totalSupply() = 1,000,000,000 LIT. balanceOf(0x…dEaD) = 18,090,720 LIT, so effective supply is 981,909,280 LIT. That equals CoinGecko's "total supply" exactly [12].

- Circulating: CoinGecko reports 250,000,000 LIT (the TGE airdrop amount, unchanged since launch). Market cap is $832M at $3.33 and FDV $3.27B (CoinGecko, 2026-11-10 16:04 UTC) [12]. The true float differs somewhat. Burns came from the reserve, not the float. Staking rewards (≥3.72M LIT paid by July 2026) and incentives have added to the float [27][29]. Treat ≈240–260M as an estimate.

- Price history: TGE 2025-12-30. ATH $7.86 (2025-12-30), ATL $0.779 (2026-03-31). 2026 local high: $5.32 (CoinGecko daily data point for 2026-09-24 00:00 UTC). Last $3.33 (−10.8% over 30 days), 24h volume $84.3M (CoinGecko, 2026-11-10 16:04 UTC). The largest venues are BitDelta, OKX, Bybit, Coinbase, MEXC, Gate and Lighter spot, plus Upbit KRW and Kraken [12].

#### Allocation and vesting

| Bucket | % / LIT | Terms | Status 2026-11-10 |

| --- | --- | --- | --- |

| Airdrop (points seasons 1–2, 12.5M points) | 25% / 250M | Fully unlocked at TGE 2025-12-30 | Circulating |

| Ecosystem (future points, partnerships, growth, staking rewards) | 25% / 250M | Discretionary; no public schedule | Likely wallet 0xe554dc…9d62 holds 231,809,274 LIT on L1. It received 249,999,995 on 2026-01-07, and both burns were sent from it. |

| Team | 26% / 260M | 1-year cliff, then 3-year linear | Locked; vesting starts ~2026-12-27/30 |

| Investors | 24% / 240M | 1-year cliff, then 3-year linear | Locked; vesting starts ~2026-12-27/30 |

Sources: the Lighter statement quoted in Cointelegraph ("The team and investors all have a 1-year unlock and 3-year linear vesting after… 26% team, 24% investor") [21]. Trackers disagree on the first vesting date. Tokenomist and CoinCentral say 2026-12-27, DefiLlama 2026-12-29, CoinLaunch 2026-12-30, and Tokenomics.com 2027-01-28 (older page). DefiLlama models about 3.19M LIT per week; CoinLaunch models 13.89M LIT per month (= 500M / 36) [26][31][32].

Custody observation (my reading of Ethereum transfers): the deployer sent 249,999,999 LIT to 0x98e7…2b5f (2025-12-20) and 249,999,999 LIT to 0xb3058a…19e4 (2025-12-22 and 2025-12-30). It sent 249,999,980 LIT to the Lighter rollup contract (airdrop, 2025-12-30) and 249,999,995 LIT to 0xe554…9d62 (2026-01-07, two transfers of 10 and 249,999,985). A further 5 LIT went to 0xc35a…50c8 (2025-12-18); the four 250M buckets plus 5 LIT account for the full 1,000,000,000 minted. The first two wallets then spread their tokens across many plain EOAs. Examples: 58.9M LIT to 0xa9f5…44e8, 51.2M to 0x47fa…b2d6, 42.4M to 0xe5fd…fa59. No on-chain vesting contract is visible. The insider lock is enforced off-chain by custody or legal agreements, so it cannot be verified on-chain. These EOAs are unlabeled; attributing them to team or investors is an inference.

