| 0xa9f5beb22c396ab05552fce0fe8b4335875e44e8 | 58,917,589 | 5.89 | EOA funded by 0x98e7 (insider bucket, inferred) |

| 0x47fa2aaa7acd628a1e72683cdb3c4d7fc9fab2d6 | 51,218,199 | 5.12 | EOA funded by 0xb3058 (inferred) |

| 0xe5fd7437d0ee86b4789a9f489ed0670b0966fa59 | 42,386,227 | 4.24 | EOA funded by 0xb3058 (inferred) |

| 0xb3058a7f08df0e252bfc012ec44314ee827019e4 | 36,116,444 | 3.61 | Received 250M from deployer |

| 0x000000000000000000000000000000000000dEaD | 18,090,720 | 1.81 | Burned |

| 0x1a51016fad47de690d1f48adf2f6407f3cdc160d | 7,698,030 | 0.77 | EOA that received the repurchased LIT withdrawn from L2 (18,090,720 in total); distributes it onward, incl. to the staking-rewards address (fact-checker read, 2026-11-10) |

The token has 12,066 L1 holders per Ethplorer [47]. Most retail LIT sits inside the Lighter L2 and is not visible as separate L1 holders.

### How it works

#### The exchange (Lighter Core)

- Architecture: an application-specific ZK rollup on Ethereum. A centralized sequencer orders transactions first-in-first-out, matches orders and runs liquidations. A custom prover produces succinct proofs that matching and liquidations followed the published rules. Proofs and compressed state diffs (as blobs) are posted to Ethereum, and Ethereum contracts hold the deposits and the canonical state root [4].

- Exit guarantees: users can push withdrawals or reduce-only orders through an Ethereum priority queue. If the sequencer ignores them, "Escape Hatch" (desert) mode freezes the contract, and users withdraw by proving their balances from blob data [4].

- Trust caveat: L2BEAT rates Lighter Stage 0. It flags "There is no delay on code upgrades (CRITICAL)", notes the security council has zeroed the notice period before every upgrade, and lists pause and emergency guardians that can freeze withdrawals for 24h or 72h. L2BEAT's total value secured is about $1.04B (2026-11-10), which includes LIT [20].

- Collateral and deposits: USDC is the main collateral, deposited via Ethereum plus bridges; Arbitrum appears in DefiLlama's TVL. Multi-asset margin is supported [6]. On-chain, the rollup contract held 564.75M USDC and 9,306.7 ETH on 2026-11-10 (RPC read, block 26,385,586).

- Markets: 490 order books are listed on mainnet (exchangeStats, 2026-11-10). They include crypto perps; RWA perps on equities, ETFs, indices, FX, gold, silver and oil, tradeable 24/7; pre-IPO and prelaunch markets; spot; and 15-minute and 1-hour BTC/ETH "Up/Down" binary options [6][7]. By rolling 24h volume on 2026-11-10 (~16:00 UTC), BTC led ($1.08B), then ETH ($632M), HYPE ($115M), XAU, US100, ZEC, SOL, QQQ, NVDA and LIT ($24M) (exchangeStats).

- LLP (Lighter Liquidity Provider): the protocol vault. It market-makes, takes over liquidations and receives liquidation fees of up to 1% of notional [5]. On 2026-11-10 (~16:00 UTC) its total account value was $99.8M with a trailing APY of 13.18% per the API (pool_info.annual_percentage_yield); DefiLlama shows $102.0M. Depositing requires staked LIT: up to 10 USDC per 1 LIT staked [1].

- Public pools: operators whitelisted by Lighter run strategies for depositors and take a performance fee [8].

#### Fees

- Standard accounts (default, retail): 0 maker / 0 taker on regular perp and spot orders, with 300 ms taker latency. TWAP/advanced orders and RFQ pay 1 bp [2].

- Premium/Advanced accounts (opt-in, for professionals and market makers): 0.40 bp maker / 2.80 bp taker with 140 ms latency. Staked LIT cuts these by 2.5% (at 1,000 LIT) up to 30% (at 500,000 LIT), giving 0.28 bp / 1.96 bp [2].

- Plus accounts: 0.5 bp maker/taker with higher rate limits [2].

- Robinhood Chain deployment (separate schedule): Standard 0/0; Plus 1.5 bp/1.5 bp; Premium 1.20 bp maker / 3.50 bp taker, falling to 0.84/2.45 bp above $500M 14-day volume. On RH, Premium tiers are based on 14-day trading volume, not on staked LIT, so LIT staking discounts do not apply there [6].

- Binary options: taker fee up to 1% × P × (1−P) per share, maker 0%. Staking discounts are up to 30% and volume discounts up to 40% [7].

- LIT Fee Credits: premium users can rent tier credit in LIT instead of staking. All proceeds are streamed to LIT stakers [3].

- Withdrawal, transfer and liquidation fees also apply. The effective take rate is very low: mainnet maker plus taker fees of $3.20M on $57.7B volume over 30 days is ≈0.55 bp (my calculation from the Lighter API).

#### Token mechanics

- Buybacks: "LIT is bought back by the protocol using trading fee revenue… via daily 24-hour TWAPs." The buyer is treasury account index 0 (L1 address shown as 0x000…000) on the LIT/USDC book [1]. Since February 2026 the treasury fills mostly as a maker [14].

- Burns: the tokenomics update of 30 Jun–1 Jul 2026 switched from holding repurchased LIT to burning it quarterly on Ethereum. Lighter said it may burn an equal amount of undistributed LIT instead of the repurchased tokens themselves, calling it "economically equivalent" [28][29]. On-chain this is what happened. Both burns came from reserve wallet 0xe554… through 0x3dd7c834…4dae to 0x…dEaD:

- 2026-07-10 22:41 UTC: 15,638,702 LIT (all buybacks through Q2 2026), tx 0x4b82f8a7…08c5f [10].

- 2026-10-09 19:37 UTC: 2,452,017 LIT (Q3 2026 buybacks), tx 0x208df37e…db4a [11].

- Plus a 1-LIT test transfer on 2026-07-10, giving 18,090,720 LIT at the dead address.

Where the repurchased LIT actually goes (fact-checker trace of Ethereum transfers): right after each burn, the same amount was withdrawn from the rollup contract to the Safe-style contract 0x3dd7c834…4dae (2026-07-10 23:24 UTC: 15,638,702 LIT; 2026-10-09 20:32 UTC: 2,452,017 LIT) and forwarded to the EOA 0x1a51016fad47de690d1f48adf2f6407f3cdc160d. That wallet has since sent out about 10.39M LIT (including 2,432,010 LIT in 20 transfers to the staking-rewards address 0xADbE…14Ff, typically 150,000 LIT a week, plus multi-hundred-thousand to 2.2M transfers to other unlabeled addresses) and held 7,698,030 LIT on 2026-11-10. So the repurchased tokens are recycled into operations and rewards, and the reserve shrinks by the burned amount. This matches Lighter's stated "equal amount of undistributed LIT" approach, but it means the "burned" tokens are not the bought tokens. Q4 buybacks are building up in treasury account 0, which held 1,618,428 LIT at ~16:00 UTC on 2026-11-10 (1,608,471 earlier the same day; buying continues daily). The original researcher summed 1,608,043 LIT of treasury buy trades since 2026-10-01, within 0.03% of the earlier balance. The next burn is expected after Q4 2026 [27].

- Staking: stake at app.lighter.xyz/staking, with a 3-day unstake lockup. Stakers get LLP access, fee discounts and a fixed 6% APR; LIT for rewards is bought from 0xADbE1265C0df1B623A56d324De494Bcb8e8914Ff [1]. Since July 2026, rewards are funded from the ecosystem reserve, not from revenue. Before that, about 3.72M LIT had been paid out of pre-TGE revenue [29]. Staked now: 101,163,821 LIT (staking pool account 281474976624800, API read 2026-11-10 ~16:00 UTC; 101,082,339 a few hours earlier). That is down from about 125M at the July announcement (Lighter) and about 110.7M on 18 Jul (Tokenomist) [27][31]. At 6% this implies about 6.1M LIT a year (~$20.2M at $3.33) paid to stakers. In practice the rewards address 0xADbE…14Ff is being topped up with recycled repurchased LIT from 0x1a51…160d (150,000 LIT a week ≈ 7.8M LIT a year at the recent pace), while an equal amount of reserve LIT is burned.

- Governance: there is no on-chain DAO or governance-vote function for LIT. Parameters, fees, buybacks and burns are company decisions announced by Lighter, and the rollup's upgrade keys sit with Lighter multisigs and a security council (L2BEAT) [20].

- Not used for: gas (L2 transactions are free for users), or as perp margin collateral; no such use is documented in the margin docs.

### Utility

| Use | Real or governance-only? | Who needs it |

| --- | --- | --- |

| Required stake to deposit into LLP (1 LIT per 10 USDC) | Real, hard requirement | Yield seekers wanting LLP's ~13% trailing APY |

| Fee discounts on Premium accounts and binary options (2.5–30%) | Real | Market makers and HFT on Premium tiers; retail Standard accounts pay 0 anyway |

| Fee Credits (rent tiers by paying LIT; proceeds go to stakers) | Real, small | Premium traders not wanting to lock LIT |

| Staking yield (6% fixed) | Real income, but paid in newly released reserve LIT (dilutive to non-stakers) | Holders |

| Claim on revenue via buyback-and-burn | Indirect (no direct cash flow); about $52M a year at the current pace | All holders |

| Governance | None in practice; no DAO | n/a |

LIT is not needed to trade on Lighter. Retail trades free with USDC, and Robinhood Wallet users trade with USDG. Demand from the product therefore comes mainly from LLP depositors, professional fee tiers and the buyback.

### Why people buy and sell it

#### Demand drivers

- Buyback-and-burn backed by revenue: about $4.29M per 30 days, a ~6.3% annualized yield on the $832M market cap (1.6% on the $3.27B FDV), CoinGecko 2026-11-10. This is a recurring market bid. On busy days it spikes, e.g. $1.40M on 28–29 Oct 2026 ($583,292 + $820,110, DefiLlama daily holders revenue) during the Binance hack sell-off.

- "Hyperliquid challenger" narrative: Lighter is #2 perp DEX by 7-day volume ($19.51B vs Hyperliquid $62.58B, week to 2026-11-08) [39], backed by Founders Fund, Ribbit, Haun and Robinhood [22].

- Robinhood: Lighter is the official perps venue on Robinhood Chain and in Robinhood Wallet (non-US), with a reported 50/50 revenue split and an incentive commitment reported as "$11 million in LIT" (Crypto Briefing, July) or "11 million LIT" (Crypto Briefing, October) — the unit is inconsistent across reports [23][25].

- Regulatory optionality: a planned CFTC filing for a DCM and a DCO in November 2026 could open US access. LIT rose 15–21% intraday on 2026-10-21 when this was announced [25][26].

- Access products and listings: Bitwise Lighter Staking ETP (BLIT, Xetra, from 2026-09-23, 0.85% TER) [35][36]; 21Shares Lighter ETP (LIHT, from 2026-10-19, 2.5% TER) [37]; Coinbase and Kraken spot (LIGHTER-USD); Upbit KRW (from 2026-08-24) [38]; Sygnum bank custody/trading access (announced Monday 2026-11-09, reported 2026-11-10) [41].

- Staking for LLP access and premium fee tiers lock about 101M LIT, roughly 40% of the 250M float.

#### Supply and sell pressure

- Insider unlock: 500M LIT (51% of effective supply) starts vesting around 27–30 Dec 2026, at about 13.9M LIT per month (~$46M per month at $3.33). Monthly buybacks are about $4.3M, so gross new insider supply is roughly 11 times the buyback bid.

- Staking emissions from the reserve: about 6.1M LIT a year at the current stake. Incentive programs: Robinhood-user incentives (reported as $11M of LIT or 11M LIT), and the ecosystem bucket also funds future points seasons [23][21].

- Airdrop overhang (largely absorbed): the 250M airdrop was the whole float at TGE. Price fell from $2.70 (2025-12-31) to $0.81 (2026-03-31) as airdropped tokens were sold [12].

- Professional short positioning: on 2026-11-09, top-100 traders across Lighter, Hyperliquid, dYdX and Pacifica were about 91% short by notional (TokenPost via CMC) [33].

### The protocol/business

- What it does: a verifiable, self-custodial, CEX-speed order-book exchange. Products: crypto perps, RWA perps (stocks, ETFs, indices, FX, metals, oil; 24/7), spot (ETH, LIT and others), binary options (from 2026-10-19), RFQ, public pools and vaults, and an EVM devnet built with Axiom (from 2026-10-16) so smart contracts can read state and place orders [6][33][34].

- Timeline: founded 2022 (a pivot from Lunchclub). Private beta from January 2025, public mainnet 2 Oct 2025 (L2BEAT), TGE 30 Dec 2025, Robinhood Chain launch 1 Jul 2026 [20][22][24].

- Audience: retail traders drawn by zero fees, airdrop and points farmers, market makers and HFT on Premium tiers, LLP yield depositors, and since July 2026 Robinhood Wallet users. Robinhood perps are unavailable in the US, UK, Canada, Switzerland, UAE and Singapore, and are aimed mainly at the EU [45]. (A circulating claim that Robinhood users are ~40% of daily active accounts could not be found in the cited CoinMarketCap page and is not used here.)

- Two separate deployments: (1) Lighter mainnet: Ethereum-settled, USDC. (2) "Lighter RH": a separate exchange on Robinhood Chain (an Arbitrum-stack L2) with chain ID 466324, USDG collateral and contract 0x94bAB9693Ba2f6358507eFfcbd372b0660AFfF9d. Accounts and balances are not shared between them [6].

