### Verification notes

Independent fact-check performed 2026-11-10 (≈15:50–16:15 UTC) against primary and on-chain sources.

#### Re-checked and confirmed

- Contract: Etherscan V2 getsourcecode shows contract Lighter, solc v0.8.25, Proxy=0; source is ERC20 + ERC20Permit with a single constructor _mint(recipient, 1_000_000_000e18) and no other mint/burn/owner functions. Created 2025-10-27 15:42 UTC by 0x004fe354…3099, minted to 0x077842a5…1891. CoinGecko lists the same Ethereum address and the Robinhood Chain address.

- Supply and burns: totalSupply() = 1,000,000,000 LIT; dead address = 18,090,720 LIT (block 26,385,586). The three dead-address transfers (1 LIT, 15,638,702 LIT on 2026-07-10 22:41 UTC, 2,452,017 LIT on 2026-10-09 19:37 UTC) and both tx hashes match. Reserve wallet arithmetic (249,999,995 in − 100,000 − 1 − 15,638,702 − 2,452,017 − 1 = 231,809,274) matches its balance. Deployer distribution (4 × ~250M + 5 LIT) matches.

- Fees/revenue/holder revenue: every DefiLlama figure (24h/7d/30d/all-time for lighter, lighter-perps, lighter-spot, lighter-robinhood-perps), the monthly trend table and the YTD row were re-queried and match exactly (data to 2026-11-09). The 7-day buyback ($870,335) was rebuilt independently from 4,307 treasury fills and matches to the dollar. The DefiLlama adapter source was read: holder revenue = account-0 buys on market 2049; liquidation fees go to supply side (LLP).

- Lighter API: mainnet 30d maker $1,593,919, taker $1,605,612, liquidation $828,574, transfer $16,340, withdrawal $3,900, volume $57.69B; 24h volume $2.71B and OI $1.062B (2026-11-09); peak OI $2.24B (2025-10-08); peak DAA 483,116 (2025-12-30); record day $18.98B (2025-09-25); monthly volumes; 490 markets. RH: 30d volume $19.06B, 7d $4.53B, OI $401M. All match.

- Docs: fee schedule, staking discounts (2.5–30%), 6% APR, 3-day lockup, 1 LIT per 10 USDC for LLP, rewards address 0xADbE…14Ff, buyback TWAP and treasury account, Fee Credits proceeds to stakers, RH chain ID 466324 and contract 0x94bA…FfF9d.

- People/funding: Fortune (2025-11-11) confirms founder/CEO Novakovski (founded 2022), Harvard at 16, Citadel at 18, Addepar, Lunchclub co-founders, 80% team retained, $68M round (Founders Fund, Ribbit, Haun, Robinhood; ~$1.5B valuation; equity + token warrants) and the $21M 2024 round (Haun, Craft; Dragonfly, Robot Ventures). Elliot Technologies (Delaware) confirmed in Crypto Briefing.

- News: Cointelegraph allocation quote; Robinhood deal (50/50 split); CFTC plan (Oct 21 call, +21.3% to $3.88 per CryptoTicker/TokenPost; vesting from Dec 27 per CoinCentral; no MiCA register entry as of 2026-11-02); binary options 2026-10-19; EVM devnet 2026-10-16; Upbit KRW 2026-08-24; Bitwise BLIT ISIN DE000A4AV9T5 (Deutsche Börse page) and 0.85% TER; 7d volume ranking; L2BEAT Stage 0 risks; Motley Fool geo-restrictions; Binance $6.3B breach.

#### Corrected

- Executive summary claimed buybacks are "roughly 95–98%" of main-exchange revenue; that holds only for Feb–Sep monthly data. In October (135%) and the latest 30 days (132%) buybacks exceeded main-exchange revenue; vs combined revenue they are ~80%. Fixed.

- Burn mechanics (material gap): on-chain tracing shows the repurchased LIT is not itself burned: after each burn of reserve LIT, the same amount is withdrawn from the rollup to Safe-style contract 0x3dd7…4dae and then to EOA 0x1a51…160d, which has redistributed ~10.39M LIT (incl. 2.43M to the staking-rewards address) and holds 7.70M. Added to sections 2, 3, 7, 8 and 11.

- Bridge TVL peak: was $1.347B on 2026-01-01; actual DefiLlama peak is $1.46B on 2025-12-18, so the drawdown is −60%, not −57%.

- Updated live values: price $3.33, market cap $832M, FDV $3.27B, 24h volume $84.3M, 30d −10.8%; rollup custody (564.75M USDC, 9,306.7 ETH, 140,706,113 LIT); staking 101,163,821 LIT; treasury 1,618,428 LIT; LLP $99.8M (APY 13.18%); L2BEAT TVS $1.04B; Hyperliquid OI $8.87B; derived yields and multiples.

- Added the separate Robinhood Chain fee schedule, where Premium tiers depend on 14-day volume and LIT staking gives no discount.

- Sygnum announcement dated Monday 2026-11-09 (reported 11-10), not 11-10. Binance freeze date "Oct 29" not supported by the cited TechCrunch article; reworded. The Robinhood $11M incentive is reported as "$11 million in LIT" in one article and "11 million LIT" in another; both shown.

- Removed two unsupported items: "Robinhood users ≈40% of daily active accounts" (not in the cited CMC page) and an unopened search-snippet fee benchmark. Noted that eGamers mislabels the Q3 burn as the "first" burn.

#### Remains unverified

- First insider vesting date (27, 29 or 30 Dec 2026): Tokenomist and DefiLlama unlock pages returned HTTP 403; the official Lighter post was not located. Insider wallet attributions remain inferences.

- 21Shares LIHT launch date and 2.5% TER (Trackinsight page is script-only); Chainlink APAC feeds story (HTTP 403); The Block pages (HTTP 403).

- Competitor market caps (HYPE, ASTER, EDGE, GMX) were not re-read (CoinGecko rate limit); their fees and holder revenue were re-checked on DefiLlama and match.

- Whether Robinhood Chain revenue is excluded from buybacks by design (50/50 split) or retained; no official disclosure found. Whether the CFTC filing has actually been submitted as of 2026-11-10 is not confirmed (the fact-checker's web-search budget was exhausted, so no new news search was possible).

- Novakovski's personal X handle was not verified.
