    ('aave:AAVE', 'https://docs.google.com/document/d/1aOUot7yVJLA6IOLvOdjEASRAYJoYhALdbxKHFN4YULw/edit', $tank_seed_AAVE_20261110$## AAVE — Aave: token & protocol fact sheet

As of 2026-11-10

The author read all on-chain values on 2026-11-10 at Ethereum block 26,385,281 (15:02:59 UTC), unless stated otherwise. "DL" means DefiLlama and "CG" means CoinGecko. USD conversions use CG/DL spot prices from 2026-11-10 at about 15:00 UTC: AAVE $124.86–125.44, ETH $2,069, BTC $74,248. DL fee and revenue windows end on the last complete UTC day (2026-11-09). An independent fact-check re-read the key values at block 26,385,551 (2026-11-10 15:57 UTC); where values moved, the fresher value is shown and the change is listed under "Verification notes".

### Executive summary

AAVE is the governance and staking token of Aave, the largest lending protocol in DeFi. Aave holds $16.2B of net TVL plus $11.8B of active loans, about 33% of all DeFi lending TVL tracked by DL. The protocol earns real cash fees: borrowers paid $39.3M over the last 30 days, and the DAO treasury kept $5.2M of that (about $63M annualized). A second check agrees: on-chain reserve-factor mints into the Ethereum Collector came to $4.05M over the same 30 days, against DL's $4.00M for Aave V3 Ethereum. Revenue does not cover the DAO's own spending plan: TokenLogic's March 2026 ARFC put an "optimistic" 2026 operating budget at $190M against 2025 revenue of $142M.

Nothing reaches AAVE holders today. The DAO-run buyback ran from 2025-04-09 and bought about $46.4M of AAVE. It has been paused since 2026-04-19, after the Kelp rsETH bridge exploit left Aave with about $124–230M of potential bad debt. To cover the gap, the DAO gave away 25,000 ETH and took a credit line of up to 30,000 ETH from Mantle. The bought-back AAVE was never burned. About 240.5K of it now sits as collateral in a DAO Safe that has borrowed 4.11M GHO against it.

The token has fallen 44.4% in a year to $122.57 and 27.3% in the last 30 days (CG, 2026-11-10 15:56 UTC; it was down 8.0% in the 24 hours to that time, in a market-wide drop with ETH down 5.7%). Protocol revenue is down about 66% year on year. The Binance hot-wallet exploit on 2026-10-29 made the selling worse, because the exploiter dumped AAVE and Aave froze 292 reserves.

The single thing to watch is whether "Aavenomics 3.0" ships. It is the promised automated, immutable buyback, possibly with a burn. It is still only an idea from the founder, with no proposal, budget or date as of 2026-11-10.

### What the token is

- Ticker: AAVE, an ERC-20 on Ethereum, a proxy at [0x7Fc66500c84A76Ad7e9c93437bFc5Ac33E2DDaE9](https://etherscan.io/token/0x7Fc66500c84A76Ad7e9c93437bFc5Ac33E2DDaE9). It was created in 2020 by migrating LEND (the 2017 ICO token) at 100 LEND : 1 AAVE.

- Staked form: stkAAVE [0x4da27a545c0c5B758a6BA100e3a049001de870f5](https://etherscan.io/address/0x4da27a545c0c5B758a6BA100e3a049001de870f5). stkAAVE carries voting power, as do aAAVE (AAVE supplied to Aave V3) and AAVE itself.

- Bridged copies: the author verified each one with symbol() and totalSupply() calls on public RPCs on 2026-11-10. The bridged supply is part of the 16M, not added to it.

- Base: [0x63706e40…f814b](https://basescan.org/token/0x63706e401c06ac8513145b7687a14804d17f814b), 36,568 AAVE.

- Arbitrum: [0xba5ddd1f…67196](https://arbiscan.io/token/0xba5ddd1f9d7f570dc94a51479a000e3bce967196), 49,731.

- Polygon: [0xd6df932a…21c90b](https://polygonscan.com/token/0xd6df932a45c0f255f85145f286ea0b292b21c90b), 61,351.

- Avalanche (AAVE.e): [0x63a72806…386d9](https://snowtrace.io/token/0x63a72806098bd3d9520cc43356dd78afe5d386d9), 7,660.

- Optimism: [0x76fb31fb…50c9278](https://optimistic.etherscan.io/token/0x76fb31fb4af56892a25e32cfc43de717950c9278), 4,832.

- BNB Chain (Binance-Peg): [0xfb611544…f802](https://bscscan.com/token/0xfb6115445bff7b52feb98650c87f44907e58f802), 400,000.

- Solana: AavE1kKKnesPw4MuRJmJ9jZs9QzEE8CPxQ3ViczUDfc1, from the CG platform list and not verified by the author.

