### Key people

- Stani Kulechov ([@StaniKulechov](https://x.com/StaniKulechov)): founder of ETHLend (2017) and Aave, and founder and CEO of Aave Labs. He authored "Aave Will Win" and is driving Aavenomics 3.0. He personally donated to DeFi United.

- Aave Labs ([@aave](https://x.com/aave), also posts as "AaveLabs" on the forum) is the DAO's development and growth service provider. It builds V4, the App, Pro and Kit, and in November 2026 acquired the Avon team (Prince Sinha, Ayush Kaul, Omar el-Ashaal). Executives named in secondary sources (RootData, 2026), not confirmed on an official Aave page:

- Linda Jeng, Chief Legal & Policy Officer, joined March 2026, formerly of the Federal Reserve and FSB.

- Luigi D'Onorio DeMeo, Chief Strategy & Business Officer, joined April 2026, formerly of Ava Labs.

- Peter Kerr, CFO.

- Nicole Butler, Chief Compliance Officer.

- Aave DAO service providers, per Governance Framework v2 (July 2026):

- LlamaRisk ([@LlamaRisk](https://x.com/LlamaRisk)): risk. It wrote the rsETH, Binance and tBTC incident reports.

- TokenLogic ([@Token_Logic](https://x.com/Token_Logic)): treasury, finance and growth. It authored the buyback pause and the emissions ARFCs.

- Certora ([@CertoraInc](https://x.com/CertoraInc)): security.

- Aave Labs: development.

- Aave Finance Committee (AFC): a multisig that executed the buybacks and holds the bought-back AAVE.

- Protocol Guardian multisig: freezes and pauses.

- Aave Foundation: proposed on 2026-10-02 as a memberless Cayman foundation to hold the Aave trademark, domains and IP, with an independent director and supervisor. Aave Labs may not appoint either role.

- Aave LLC received the court-cleared Arbitrum ETH in the rsETH recovery.

- Departures in 2026:

- BGD Labs (Ernesto Boado [@eboadom](https://x.com/eboadom), Emilio Frangella [@The3D_](https://x.com/The3D_)), the core V3 engineers, announced its departure on 2026-02-20 citing disagreements over direction, particularly V4 ([The Defiant](https://thedefiant.io/news/defi/bgd-to-leave-aave-citing-governance-tensions)). The 2026-04-01 end date of the engagement is from the original draft and was not independently re-verified.

- Chaos Labs (Omer Goldberg), the risk provider, announced its exit on about 2026-04-07. Goldberg said V4 migration risks were more than it would assume and that it was "walking away from a $5 million engagement"; Kulechov said Aave had offered to double the payment to $5M and that Chaos wanted to be the sole risk provider and use its own oracles instead of Chainlink ([Cointelegraph](https://cointelegraph.com/news/defi-risk-manager-chaos-labs-leaves-aave-says-decision-not-made-haste)).

- Aave Chan Initiative (Marc Zeller, [@lemiscate](https://x.com/lemiscate)), the largest governance delegate/service provider, announced its exit in March 2026 and wound down by about July. It alleged that Labs-linked addresses decided the funding vote.

### Recent news (last ~90 days)

- 2026-09: early access to the Aave App (via "Ghost Pass" drops) expands, including drops for US users, and USDC/USDT are enabled on Ethereum. In October deposits go live from BNB Chain, HyperEVM and Monad ([AL September update](https://governance.aave.com/t/al-development-update-september-2026/25744)).

- 2026-09-16: Aave V4 launches on Circle's Arc.

- 2026-09-22: analysis by Chado/Odaily: buybacks are unlikely to resume soon. DAO revenue is about $167K/day, and repaying the Mantle facility would take about 473 days ([KuCoin/Odaily](https://www.kucoin.com/news/flash/aave-s-repurchase-stalled-473-days-needed-to-repay-loan)).

- 2026-09-25 / 2026-10-07: the Snapshot vote to deploy V4 on Base passes (2026-09-25), and the V4 Equities Hub on Base goes live on 2026-10-07 ([changelog](https://aave.com/docs/resources/changelog)). Non-US users borrow USDC against tokenized stocks. By late October: more than $9M of deposits and about $4M of loans.

- 2026-09-28: Kulechov says a burn is being considered for Aavenomics 3.0, and AAVE rises about 11%.

- 2026-10-02 / 2026-10-10: [ARFC: The Aave Foundation, Phase 1](https://governance.aave.com/t/arfc-the-aave-foundation-phase-1/25756) is published; it passes Snapshot on 2026-10-10 (572,726 for, 0 against).

- 2026-10: Sentora goes live as the first external curator on V4 (the DAO gets 50% of revenue). V4 deposits pass $1.5B. The liquidation protocol fee is raised for WBTC, WETH and wstETH. Oracle deprecation for long-tail assets.

- 2026-10-14 → 2026-11-09: the ARFC to onboard native BTC as collateral on V4 via Babylon Trustless Bitcoin Vaults passes Snapshot (vote 2026-11-06 14:03 to 2026-11-09 14:03 UTC, 356,881 for, 0 against). An on-chain AIP is still required. Mainnet is targeted by the end of 2026 ([ARFC](https://governance.aave.com/t/arfc-onboard-native-btc-as-collateral-to-aave-v4-via-babylon-trustless-bitcoin-vaults/25845), [TokenPost](https://tokenpost.com/news/technology/53076)).

- 2026-10-21 / 2026-10-31: ARFC for Aave V3.8, a security-focused release under a Business Source License; it passed Snapshot on 2026-10-31 (381,439 for, 0 against) and goes to audits before the AIP. The ARFC to deploy V4 on Tempo passed Snapshot the same day (381,423 for).

- 2026-10-26 / 11-02: Aave Labs, Kamino and Veda submit a confidential framework to the SEC arguing that DeFi lending and non-custodial vaults are not securities. A public summary follows on 2026-11-02 ([Crypto Briefing](https://cryptobriefing.com/aave-kamino-veda-defi-lending-framework-sec/)).

- 2026-10-29: Binance hot-wallet exploit (about 195K ETH drained).

- One exploiter wallet supplied 60M USDT on Aave and borrowed 19,762 WETH. The position is over-collateralized.

- The guardian froze 175 reserves on V3 across 16 networks and 117 reserves on V4.

- The exploiter sold AAVE, and AAVE fell about 9% ([LlamaRisk](https://governance.aave.com/t/binance-hot-wallet-exploit-aaves-response/25954)).

- As of 2026-11-09, users still report stablecoin LTV at 0 on V3 and USDC at 0 on V4 Arc.

- 2026-10-31: tBTC freeze on V3 Ethereum Core after Threshold paused minting. Threshold restored operations on 2026-11-09, and an unfreeze is pending; on-chain the tBTC reserve is still frozen at block 26,385,551 (fact-checker getConfiguration read) ([forum](https://governance.aave.com/t/tbtc-mint-redeem-pause-aaves-response/25965)).

- 2026-11-02: AL October update: $1.1T all-time borrow volume, and V4 deposits above $1.5B with loans above $450M.

- 2026-11-05: Payward (Kraken) discloses open-market AAVE purchases of undisclosed size.

- 2026-11-06: Aave Labs acquires the Avon team and technology (fixed-rate lending and an on-chain order book). No launch date has been given ([Crypto Briefing](https://cryptobriefing.com/aave-labs-acquires-avon-fixed-rate-lending/)).

- 2026-11-09: TEMP CHECK "Aave Security Shield", on preventive controls for external incidents, is opened ([forum](https://governance.aave.com/t/26124)).

- 2026-11-10: Threshold confirms on the Aave forum that tBTC minting and redemptions are live again; a cirBTC (Circle Wrapped Bitcoin) assessment for Aave Ethereum is posted ([forum](https://governance.aave.com/t/26179)). AAVE trades at $122.57, down 8.0% in 24 hours, alongside ETH −5.7% and BTC −3.0% (CG, 15:56 UTC); no Aave-specific trigger was found on the forum.

Context from earlier in 2026:

- 2026-03-30: V4 launches.

- 2026-04-12: "Aave Will Win" funding vote passes.

- 2026-04-18: rsETH exploit. Of the 116,500 rsETH drained, 89,567 were deposited on Aave against 82,650 WETH borrowed.

- 2026-04-19: buybacks paused.

- 2026-04-23: DeFi United launched.

- 2026-05-06: the attacker's positions are liquidated via an AIP.

- 2026-05-09: WETH is unfrozen and the court clears the $71M transfer of Arbitrum-frozen ETH to Aave LLC.

- 2026-06-26: Kraken stake-talk report, which Kulechov denies.

### Current problems and risks

- No value accrual. Buybacks have been at $0 for 205 days (2026-04-19 to 2026-11-10). The previously bought AAVE was not burned and is now pledged as collateral. Aavenomics 3.0 exists only as founder tweets.

- Shrinking revenue. DAO revenue was $5.20M over 30 days against $15.09M in October 2025 (-66%), and fees fell from $114.8M to $39.7M per month. TVL is $16.2B against a $43.3B peak (-63%). The Block notes Aave TVL is down nearly half in 2026.

- Balance-sheet repair. The DAO gave away 25,000 ETH, has a Mantle facility of up to 30,000 ETH, and its GHO borrow against treasury AAVE stands at 4.11M. More than 50% of the treasury is AAVE itself (forum, May 2026). That is reflexive: a falling AAVE price shrinks the treasury.

- Contagion from external assets. rsETH (April), the Binance exploit (October) and tBTC (October/November) all forced broad freezes. Frozen markets and zero stablecoin LTVs hurt usability and push users to competitors. Forum users openly ask to "shut down Aave already". The proposed "Security Shield" is a response.

- Competition. Morpho has $11.0B TVL (22.8% share) and charges no protocol fee. Spark has $4.6B and Maple $2.3B. Curated-vault models are eating into Aave's share. V4's curated hubs are Aave's answer.

- Governance centralization and talent loss. BGD, Chaos Labs and ACI left. Aave Labs is now the dominant provider and also holds a large undisclosed AAVE stake, which ACI says was decisive in the funding vote. The service-provider set is now small: Labs, LlamaRisk, TokenLogic and Certora.

- Overhang: Labs' AAVE allocation being discussed with buyers, and stkAAVE outflows. Four large stakers exited in Q2 2026 (TokenLogic).

- Oracle and configuration risk. On 2026-03-10/12 a CAPO wstETH snapshot misconfiguration caused about $862K of wrongful liquidations, which were reimbursed (DL hacks list).

- Legal: terrorism-judgment creditors (DPRK) keep a claim on the $71M of ETH transferred to Aave LLC ([The Block](https://www.theblock.co/news/ecosystems/2026-05-09-arbitrums-71-million-in-eth-cleared-for-aave-transfer-as-north-korea-terrorism-creditors-retain-legal-claim-400642)).

What the market still believes in:

- Aave remains the default DeFi credit layer.

- V4 plus institutional distribution (Circle Arc, Coinbase Base equities, Kraken/Payward, Babylon BTC, Privy and fintech "earn") can return revenue to growth.

- Once the Mantle facility is cleared, an automated buyback-and-burn would turn the $60–90M/yr revenue run-rate into direct token demand.

### What would move the token

| Catalyst | Timing | Bullish if | Bearish if |

| --- | --- | --- | --- |

| Aavenomics 3.0 ARFC (automated buyback, possible burn, staking role) | Not scheduled. Promised since 2026-06-25. | A fixed share of revenue goes to on-chain buybacks with a burn, and possibly the existing 240K+ treasury AAVE is burned. | Further delay, a small budget (below the $30M/yr previously proposed), or tokens kept in the treasury. |

| Restoring stablecoin LTV and lifting the Binance/tBTC freezes | Pending (November 2026) | Quick, complete unfreeze and borrowing recovery. | Prolonged restrictions and user migration. |

| Mantle facility repayment and treasury disclosure | Ongoing, up to 36 months | Early repayment, a published wallet list, a clean balance sheet. | A larger-than-expected drawn balance. |

| Babylon native-BTC spokes on V4 | Mainnet targeted by end of 2026 | Meaningful BTC collateral inflow and WBTC borrow demand. | Delays or small caps (initial capacity about $21M of stablecoins reported). |

| Aave V3.8 AIP (ARFC passed 2026-10-31, audits pending); V4 on Tempo (ARFC passed 2026-10-31); fixed-rate (Avon) product | Q4 2026 – 2027 | V4 deposits keep compounding from $1.5B. | Security incidents in the new code. |

| Aave Foundation Phase 1 implementation (IP and trademark to a memberless foundation) | ARFC passed Snapshot 2026-10-10; incorporation and director appointments pending | Clearer token-centric ownership. | Renewed Labs/DAO conflict. |

| Payward/Kraken further purchases; sale of the Labs AAVE allocation | Open | Strategic buyers at or above market. | A discounted OTC sale (the June report implied a 70% discount). |

| Borrow-rate environment and crypto beta | Continuous | Rising leverage demand. Revenue is very sensitive to ETH/stablecoin borrow utilization. | Further deleveraging. |

