    ('morpho:MORPHO', 'https://docs.google.com/document/d/1f6lBGhF92QhATvpJnGaoYTmi2y9zGaBdGt18-KZGVJ0/edit', $tank_seed_MORPHO_20261110$## MORPHO — Morpho: token & protocol fact sheet

As of 2026-11-10

### Executive summary

MORPHO is the governance token of Morpho, the second-largest EVM lending network after Aave. Morpho has three parts: Morpho Blue, an immutable layer of isolated variable-rate lending markets; Morpho Midnight, fixed-rate and fixed-term markets live since July 2026; and Morpho Vaults, through which third-party curators allocate deposits. No value reaches token holders today. Users paid about $28.0M in interest over the last 30 days and $209M over the last 12 months (DefiLlama). Protocol revenue and holder revenue are both $0. I confirmed this on-chain: on Ethereum and Base, Morpho Blue feeRecipient() returns the zero address, every top market has fee = 0, and Ethereum has no SetFee event since deployment, and none of the 714 listed Blue markets in the Morpho API has a non-zero fee. The Morpho Association (a French non-profit that owns Morpho Labs) publicly argues that any future fees should be reinvested rather than distributed.

The business is growing fast and is the main source of the hype. Borrowing on Morpho rose 63% in 12 months to $5.70B (DefiLlama, 2026-11-10), and the company reports $17B in deposits (ATH, Oct 2026). Coinbase, Robinhood Chain, Circle's Arc, Ledger, Bitwise and Apollo all build on it, and a $175M token raise closed in June 2026. The token has not followed the business: it trades at $2.00 (CoinGecko, 2026-11-10 15:59 UTC), down 18.5% over 30 days and 52% below its January 2025 ATH of $4.17. The main things to watch are (1) whether governance ever turns on the Blue fee switch or the Midnight fees, and who receives them, and (2) supply: about 30% of supply is not yet circulating, the Association received a new 150M MORPHO grant in April 2026, and insider vesting runs to late 2027.

### What the token is

- Ticker: MORPHO (CoinGecko id morpho, rank #62 on 2026-11-10). Spot markets on Binance, Coinbase, Upbit and others; USDT perpetuals on Binance and Bybit.

- Type: governance token only. No fee rights, no staking yield, not used as gas.

- Two token contracts on Ethereum:

- Wrapped MORPHO, the transferable token traded on exchanges: 0x58D97B57BB95320F9a05dC918Aef65434969c2B2.

- Legacy MORPHO, immutable and convertible 1:1 through the wrapper contract 0x9D03bb2092270648d7480049d0E58d2FcF0E5123: 0x9994E35Db50125E0DF82e4c2dde62496CE330999.

Only wrapped MORPHO is transferable; the wrapper was created for on-chain vote tracking under MIP-75 ([docs](https://docs.morpho.org/governance/morpho-token/overview)).

- Bridged deployments:

- Base: 0xBAa5CC21fd487B8Fcc2F632f3F4E8D37262a0842, with 25,754,564 MORPHO supply read on-chain on 2026-11-10.

- Arbitrum (LayerZero OFT, MIP-113): 0x40BD670A58238e6E230c430BBb5cE6ec0d40df48.

- Katana: 0x1e5eFCA3D0dB2c6d5C67a4491845c43253eB9e4e.

- HyperEVM (MIP-118).

I took the addresses from CoinGecko platforms and checked the Ethereum and Base ones with totalSupply().

