How the two contracts add up (on-chain, 2026-11-10): wrapped totalSupply() = 999,999,999.8 and legacy totalSupply() = 999,999,993.2, but they are not additive. The wrapper contract 0x9D03…5123 holds 618,106,278 legacy MORPHO (already converted) and 381,893,722 pre-minted wrapped MORPHO (reserved for legacy tokens not yet converted). Economic supply is therefore 1B: ~618.1M wrapped in circulation plus ~381.9M still in legacy form. The Base supply (25.75M) is bridged from Ethereum and is also not additive.

About 620M MORPHO sit outside these three addresses. That figure includes founders, strategic partners, contributors, exchanges and users. I could not get a full holder ranking: the Etherscan holder-list endpoint needs a paid plan.

