Morpho has about 23.6% of borrows across these eight lenders ($5.70B of $24.2B). That fits the company's claim that "one in every five dollars borrowed onchain is borrowed through Morpho" (Oct 2026). AAVE market cap is $1.89B, against MORPHO's $1.41B (FDV $2.00B) (CoinGecko, 2026-11-10).

#### Audience and where it is popular

- Coinbase users on Base are the biggest single source of borrowing. Coinbase Borrow runs on Morpho for BTC, ETH, XRP, SOL and, since 2026-11-06, PAXG. Coinbase Lend for USDC passed $500M. Fixed-rate loans through Midnight started 2026-09-22. The listed USDC/PAXG market on Base (77% LLTV) was still small on 2026-11-10: $36.9k supplied, $33.3k borrowed (Morpho API).

- Robinhood Chain: Robinhood Earn passed $500M; USDG markets; Robinhood Stock Tokens accepted as collateral since October 2026 (Oct newsletter, published 2026-11-05).

- Circle Arc (live 2026-09-16; cirBTC/USDC; Circle Mint Digital Asset Borrow, about $200M borrowed in under 2 weeks). USDC is Morpho's core asset: $3.98B of USDC supplied to listed Blue markets on 2026-11-10 (Morpho API, my sum; excludes idle vault cash).

- Institutional curators and RWA issuers: Bitwise, Sentora, Steakhouse, Grove, PayPal USD (PYUSD) vault, Ripple RLUSD (Sentora x Spark RLUSD vault $500M), Paxos USDG ($500M+), Société Générale (EURCV).

- Regions: mainly US users through Coinbase and Robinhood (PAXG loans for eligible US users excluding New York, per Crypto Briefing); the company is in Paris; APAC via SoSoValue; Mexico via Bitso (MXN yield, reported 2026-10-27, single secondary source).

