### Revenue and value capture

| Layer | 24h | 7d | 30d | 12 months | All-time | Source / note |

| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |

| (a) Gross fees paid by users (borrow interest plus liquidation bonuses) | $0.92M (last full UTC day, 2026-11-09: Blue $0.910M + Midnight $8.0k; the partial 2026-11-10 shows $0.81M) | $8.00M | $27.98M | $209.3M | $393.3M | DefiLlama morpho, 2026-11-10 |

| of which Midnight | $8.0k (2026-11-09) | $0.11M | $0.53M | $0.57M | — | DefiLlama morpho-midnight |

| (a') Interest run-rate, independent check | $299.5M annualized (~$820k/day) = Σ(borrowAssetsUsd × borrowApy) over 714 listed markets (first read: $297.2M over 703 markets) |  |  |  |  | Morpho API, my calculation, 2026-11-10 |

| (b) Protocol revenue | $0 | $0 | $0 | $0 | $0 | DefiLlama dailyRevenue; on-chain fee = 0 |

| (c) Value to MORPHO holders (buyback, burn, distribution) | $0 | $0 | $0 | $0 | $0 | DefiLlama dailyHoldersRevenue; no such mechanism exists |

| Curator fees (to curators, not the protocol) | ~$20M a year, estimate: V1 ~ $4.1M + V2 ~ $16.1M, from current TVL × APY × fee rates |  |  |  |  | Morpho API, my calculation |

- Annualizations and trend:

- The 30d figure annualizes to about $340M and the 7d figure to about $417M. The 7d number is inflated by liquidation-heavy days: $1.29M on 2026-11-05 and $1.84M on 2026-11-08.

- The trailing 12 months ($209M) are lower because borrowing grew through the year.

- Monthly Blue fees: Oct 2025 $24.1M; Dec 2025 $12.3M; Mar 2026 $11.3M; Jun 2026 $18.8M; Sep 2026 $19.6M; Oct 2026 $25.4M (DefiLlama monthly sums).

- Why the two sources differ: DefiLlama counts interest plus liquidation bonuses actually accrued per day. The API run-rate is an instantaneous snapshot at current APYs and covers listed markets only. Both put current gross interest at about $0.8–0.9M a day.

- Exact mechanism, on-chain:

- In Morpho Blue, setFee(MarketParams, newFee) (owner only, max 25%) would mint supply shares to feeRecipient on each interest accrual. On 2026-11-10, feeRecipient() = 0x000…000 on Ethereum and Base, and market(id).fee = 0 for the largest markets. Etherscan getLogs shows zero SetFee and zero SetFeeRecipient events on Ethereum since deployment (block 18,883,124).

- Midnight fees are disabled (see above). DefiLlama's methodology also says "Both are disabled at launch, so Revenue is currently 0."

- Holder P/F: MORPHO's FDV ($2.00B) is about 6.7× the gross-interest run-rate ($299.5M), but P/E is undefined because revenue is $0.

- Plans to monetize:

- The Association's stated position (Paul Frambot, "Aligning Around MORPHO", 2025-06-06): "As the Morpho DAO explores introducing protocol fees… the Morpho Association advocates for reinvesting protocol fees rather than distributing them." The same post made Morpho Labs SAS a wholly owned subsidiary of the Association, so no equity holders sit beside the token.

- Fee switch history: no Snapshot vote to activate the Blue fee switch has ever been held. I checked the 40 most recent proposals, MIP-96 to MIP-135. Four Pillars reports none among 128 votes up to Mar 2026.

- MIP-94 (Feb 2025) redirected Berachain license fees to the Association, citing tax risk for token holders. The amount was not disclosed.

- Association revenue: what the Association or Morpho Labs earns commercially (integration or licensing deals) is not available. It publishes no financial statements.

### How to verify on-chain

All values below were read on 2026-11-10 (first pass: Ethereum block 26,385,283, Base block 55,663,198; fact-check re-run: Ethereum block 26,385,575, Base block 55,680,727). Every command below was re-run and returned the stated result. Replace YOUR_KEY with your own Etherscan key. Note: the free Etherscan tier does not serve Base (chainid 8453); use a Base RPC eth_getLogs in block ranges instead.

#### 1. Blue fee recipient and owner

Expected: feeRecipient = zero address, so the fee switch is off; owner = 0xcba2…9afa (DAO multisig). For Base, use https://base-rpc.publicnode.com; the result is the same.

curl -s https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com -H 'content-type: application/json' \ -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_call","params":[{"to":"0xBBBBBbbBBb9cC5e90e3b3Af64bdAF62C37EEFFCb","data":"0x46904840"},"latest"]}'# owner(): data "0x8da5cb5b"

#### 2. Per-market fee and size

market(bytes32) = 0x5c60e39a. It returns 6 words: totalSupplyAssets, totalSupplyShares, totalBorrowAssets, totalBorrowShares, lastUpdate, fee. Base cbBTC/USDC returned supply 1,906,724,341 USDC and borrow 1,620,488,045 USDC on the first pass, and 1,887,991,816 / 1,619,316,890 USDC on the re-run (Base block 55,680,727); fee 0 both times.

curl -s https://base-rpc.publicnode.com -H 'content-type: application/json' \ -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_call","params":[{"to":"0xBBBBBbbBBb9cC5e90e3b3Af64bdAF62C37EEFFCb","data":"0x5c60e39a9103c3b4e834476c9a62ea009ba2c884ee42e94e6e314a26f04d312434191836"},"latest"]}'

#### 3. Fee-switch history

SetFee(bytes32,uint256) topic 0x139d6f58e9a127229667c8e3b36e88890a66cfc8ab1024ddc513e189e125b75b; SetFeeRecipient(address) topic 0x2e979f80fe4d43055c584cf4a8467c55875ea36728fc37176c05acd784eb7a73. Result: no records for either (re-checked 2026-11-10). As a sanity check, EnableLltv (topic 0x297b80e7…9139) returns 9 events. Contract creation block: 18,883,124 (2023-12-28).

curl -s "https://api.etherscan.io/v2/api?chainid=1&module=logs&action=getLogs&address=0xBBBBBbbBBb9cC5e90e3b3Af64bdAF62C37EEFFCb&topic0=0x139d6f58e9a127229667c8e3b36e88890a66cfc8ab1024ddc513e189e125b75b&fromBlock=0&toBlock=latest&apikey=YOUR_KEY"

#### 4. Midnight fees

On Ethereum, feeClaimer() (0x81cbd3ea) and feeSetter() (0x87cf3ef4) returned 0x0, and defaultContinuousFee(USDC) (0x265d32c1) returned 0. All three selectors appear in the contract bytecode, and an unknown selector reverts, so the zeros are real values, not a fallback.

curl -s https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com -H 'content-type: application/json' \ -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_call","params":[{"to":"0x471686c42792F93528B000beF54bC10E3aa2045f","data":"0x81cbd3ea"},"latest"]}'

#### 5. Treasury balances

balanceOf = 0x70a08231 + padded address. Query both the legacy token (0x9994E35D…0999) and the wrapped token (0x58D97B57…c2B2). The call below checks the DAO's legacy balance and returned 287,155,495.66 MORPHO. Use the same call for the Association (0x6ABfd613…F6a2).

curl -s https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com -H 'content-type: application/json' \ -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_call","params":[{"to":"0x9994E35Db50125E0DF82e4c2dde62496CE330999","data":"0x70a08231000000000000000000000000cba28b38103307ec8da98377fff9816c164f9afa"},"latest"]}'

#### 6. Token flows (DAO and Association)

The MIP-131 150M transfer is tx 0x95cc7c98…d571.

curl -s "https://api.etherscan.io/v2/api?chainid=1&module=account&action=tokentx&contractaddress=0x58D97B57BB95320F9a05dC918Aef65434969c2B2&address=0x6ABfd6139c7C3CC270ee2Ce132E309F59cAaF6a2&sort=desc&apikey=YOUR_KEY"

#### 7. Fees, revenue and holder revenue (DefiLlama)

curl -s "https://api.llama.fi/summary/fees/morpho?dataType=dailyFees"curl -s "https://api.llama.fi/summary/fees/morpho?dataType=dailyRevenue"curl -s "https://api.llama.fi/summary/fees/morpho?dataType=dailyHoldersRevenue"curl -s "https://api.llama.fi/protocol/morpho"   # currentChainTvls incl. "borrowed"

#### 8. Interest run-rate (Morpho API)

Run this query, then sum borrowAssetsUsd × borrowApy over all items, paging with skip. Result: $299.5M a year over 714 markets (re-run 2026-11-10); 0 listed markets had a non-zero fee. Do not drop where:{listed:true}: unlisted spam markets report absurd USD values.

curl -s https://blue-api.morpho.org/graphql -H 'content-type: application/json' \ -d '{"query":"{ markets(first:500, where:{listed:true}) { items { marketId state { supplyAssetsUsd borrowAssetsUsd borrowApy fee } } } }"}'

#### 9. DAO multisig threshold

getThreshold() = 0xe75235b8 returned 6; getOwners() = 0xa0e67e2b returned 10 addresses.

curl -s https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com -H 'content-type: application/json' \ -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_call","params":[{"to":"0xcBa28b38103307Ec8dA98377ffF9816C164f9AFa","data":"0xe75235b8"},"latest"]}'

#### 10. Governance votes

curl -s https://hub.snapshot.org/graphql -H 'content-type: application/json' \ -d '{"query":"{ proposals(first:20, where:{space_in:[\"morpho.eth\"]}, orderBy:\"created\", orderDirection:desc){ title state end scores } }"}'

