### Current problems and risks

- No value accrual, and the issuer prefers it that way. All interest goes to lenders and curators. The Association, the token's largest active spender, argues for reinvestment, and the DAO has never voted on a fee switch. The 2026-09-26 deleted-post episode publicly showed how thin vault economics are, even for curators.

- Treasury dilution and Association discretion.

- In April 2026 the DAO (4.34M votes For, about 0.4% of supply) gave the Association 150M MORPHO, 15% of supply, for 2026–2030. Since then the Association has moved tens of millions out to unlabeled wallets.

- The Apollo deal and the $175M sale were negotiated by the Association, not voted by the DAO.

- Voting power is concentrated among a few delegates; Stake Capital typically casts 73–82% of votes cast.

- Curator and collateral risk ("isolation" still loses money for someone).

- Resolv (Mar 2026): hardcoded oracle, about 15 vaults hit.

- msY (Jun 2026): about $18M lost in a single vault.

- Earlier, the Stream Finance / Elixir deUSD collapse (Nov 2025) also hit some curator vaults; not re-verified for this report.

- Exotic collateral (tokenized stocks, PAXG with weekend price freezes, receivables) adds oracle and legal risk.

The Morpho API flags very large "bad debt" on several unlisted spam markets with nonsensical USD pricing. These are not listed vaults, but they show how permissionless the market list is.

- Concentration on Coinbase and Base. One market, Base cbBTC/USDC, holds $1.62B, about 29% of all listed borrows. Coinbase's integration accounts for $1.7B+ of loans. A change in Coinbase's strategy, or an in-house lending stack, is a single point of failure for the growth story.

- Token price lags the fundamentals. The token is -18.5% over 30 days and -52% from ATH (2026-11-10) while borrows are near their high. Unlock overhang from Cohort 3 strategic partners (about 2.8M a month), possibly founders, DAO incentives and Association spending caps the upside.

- Competition. Aave V4 and Horizon (RWA); Spark ($6.2B TVL, Sky-backed); Maple in institutional credit; Euler and Fluid in modular lending. After Kelp, Aave's share of lending TVL fell from about 49.5% to 35.4% (Spartan Group / DefiLlama, Apr 2026), which helps Morpho, but Aave remains twice Morpho's borrow book.

- Regulatory: US curators, Coinbase and Robinhood products depend on how the SEC treats "vaults" (Hester Peirce statement, July 2026). Morpho's own lobbying for a noncustodial classification shows the issue is still open.

- What is going well: borrows +63% year on year; new chains ramp quickly (Arc $500M in 2 weeks, Robinhood Chain $1B in 3 months); Midnight is gaining adoption (Coinbase fixed-rate loans, $200M+ deposits); blue-chip partners. The market's belief is that Morpho becomes the default back end for fintech and bank lending, the "AWS of on-chain credit".

### What would move the token

| Date | Catalyst | Bullish if | Bearish if |

| --- | --- | --- | --- |

| 2026-11-13 | MIP-135 Snapshot vote ends (11 new Midnight LLTVs) | Passes; more Midnight market types | Minor either way |

| Q4 2026 | Midnight Adapter: Vaults V2 (~$5B) can allocate to fixed-rate markets | Midnight deposits scale from $0.2B to $1B+ | Delays or a security incident |

| "Soon" (company, Oct 2026) | First receivables-backed credit markets; more stock-token collateral | Named payment or fintech partner with real volume | Legal or oracle problems with off-chain collateral |

| Ongoing to 2027-11-21 | Strategic-partner Cohort 3 vesting (~2.8M MORPHO/month); founders' vesting possibly to Nov 2027 (May 2028 at most) | Absorbed by Apollo or strategic buying | Exchange inflows from insider wallets |

| 2026–2030 | Apollo buying up to 90M MORPHO (from 2026-02-13); Association spending of the 150M MIP-131 grant | Visible accumulation | Association transfers to exchanges or market makers |

| Any time | Fee-switch proposal on Blue or activation of Midnight fees, and the choice of recipient | Fees routed to DAO or holders: buyback, staking, distribution | Fees routed only to the Association, or a vote rejects it |

| Ongoing | Coinbase, Robinhood, Circle and other integrations; Morpho deposits vs Aave | New tier-1 distributor; borrows above $6–7B | A large partner leaves; curator blow-up; bad debt in a flagship vault |

