As of 2026-11-10. On-chain reads were taken at Ethereum block ~26,385,282 (2026-11-10, ~15:00 UTC) unless stated otherwise. Market data is from CoinGecko at 2026-11-10 16:05 UTC (refreshed by the fact-checker); DefiLlama TVL refreshed at ~16:00 UTC. "Net TVL" means supplied minus borrowed, as DefiLlama defines it. "Gross deposits" means idle cash plus outstanding loans.

### Executive summary

EUL is the governance and incentive token of Euler, a modular lending protocol. In Euler V2 anyone can deploy an ERC-4626 lending vault (EVK), and the Ethereum Vault Connector (EVC) links vaults so they can act as collateral for one another. Today nothing reaches EUL holders. Euler Labs proposed cutting protocol fees to zero on 2026-04-29. The multisig set the global default protocol fee share from 50% to 0% on Ethereum and Avalanche on 2026-05-12 (verified on-chain; per-vault 50% overrides remain on some legacy vaults). The Fee Flow buyback made its last EUL purchase on 2026-04-11. DefiLlama shows $0.29 of holder revenue over the last 30 days and $2,704 of protocol revenue. The protocol is in a post-crisis reset, not a growth phase. Gross deposits peaked at $4.21B (2025-10-07). Net TVL is now $252.7M (DefiLlama, 2026-11-10) and the market cap is $21.6M (CoinGecko, 2026-11-10 16:05 UTC). Both co-founders left Euler Labs in early 2026, and the team was restructured. About $196M of the remaining ~$324M in loans sits in vaults that are 100% utilized with zero cash. These are mostly legacy markets from the Stream Finance and Resolv crises on Plasma, Avalanche, Sonic and Ethereum. The live book is now concentrated on Monad, where one curator, K3 Capital, manages ~58% of deposits. The single most important thing to watch is whether the DAO switches protocol fees and Fee Flow back on, and against what level of healthy, fee-paying borrowing. Healthy borrowing is ~$128M today. Until fees return, EUL is a governance claim on a ~$4.3M main Treasury Safe (of which ~$3.7M is its own EUL and only ~$0.68M is USDC/ETH, valued 2026-11-10) and on a fee switch that is turned off. A secondary watch item is the 2.718%/year inflation mint, which has been callable since 2026-01-01 but has not been used.

### What the token is

- Ticker / name: EUL / Euler. ERC-20 with ERC20Votes (delegation) and AccessControl, contract name Eul, Solidity 0.8.4, verified on Etherscan.

- Canonical contract (Ethereum): 0xd9Fcd98c322942075A5C3860693e9f4f03AAE07b. Verified via Etherscan source and the official [euler-interfaces TokenAddresses.json](https://github.com/euler-xyz/euler-interfaces/blob/master/addresses/1/TokenAddresses.json).

- Other chains: bridged with LayerZero OFT. The Ethereum OFT adapter 0x4d7e09f73843bd4735aaf7a74b6d877bac75a531 (Etherscan label "Euler: OFT Adapter") holds 441,286 EUL that back supply on other chains. Addresses per CoinGecko, cross-checked against euler-interfaces for Avalanche, Monad, Base, BSC, Sonic and Plasma:

- Arbitrum 0x462cd9e0247b2e63831c3189ae738e5e9a5a4b64

