- The protocol accrued $51.7K on $2.0M of interest.

- Last buyback was 2026-04-11, with $3.2M cumulative ([forum](https://forum.euler.finance/t/euler-in-august-2026-monad-ended-the-month-larger-than-ethereum-deposits-fell-2-7-at-augus/1869)).

- 2026-09-03 → 09-09: K3 Capital's Ethereum stablecoin cluster unwound. Borrows fell from $204.7M at block 25,878,704 (2026-09-01) to ~$1.2M today. The vaults were eRLUSD-7, ePYUSD-6, eUSDC-70 and eUSDC-80, all with governor 0x060d…fea3 = K3 Capital. As a result, DefiLlama Ethereum borrowed fell from $243M to $39M in September. The reason was not publicly stated (on-chain reads).

- 2026-09-02/03: Laser Digital (Nomura) and Keyring announced institutional fixed-income lending markets prepared for Euler. Laser Digital will be the risk governor. No launch date, capital or fees were disclosed ([crypto.news](https://crypto.news/laser-digital-and-keyring-bring-institutional-fixed-income-markets-to-euler/)).

- 2026-08-22: per Datum, DefiLlama's Euler fee adapter stopped publishing. DefiLlama has since backfilled 08-23 → 09-02 with roughly double the preceding daily values, so treat that window as unreliable.

- 2026-08-09: a forum post announced an ungoverned kUSD/USDC isolated market on Euler Base. In July there were proposals for kUSD/USDC and eFIXDI/USDC (a tokenized Brazilian DI fund) ([forum](https://forum.euler.finance/c/euler-dao/34)).

- 2026-07-26 (context, just outside the 90 days): Upbit listed EUL/KRW. The price went from $1.09 to $2.29 in two days and volume from ~$3M to $178M/day, then retraced.

- Earlier 2026 context:

- 2026-06-11: Unlink privacy integration.

- 2026-06-01: Securitize permissioned vaults.

- ~2026-05-28: VanEck tokenized fund on Euler (CoinDesk).

- 2026-05-15: Euler takes over HyperEVM coverage from HypurrFi.

- 2026-05-12: default protocol fee share set from 50% to 0 on Ethereum (tx 0xc8824b77…) and Avalanche (tx 0x51874489…), and on Monad per Datum; per-vault 50% overrides remain on some legacy vaults.

- 2026-04-29: proposal to cut fees to zero.

- 2026-04-10: DAO-managed markets sunset.

- 2026-04-07: Q1 retrospective.

- March 2026: the Resolv exploit hit base-layer markets.

- 2026-01-12: CEO succession announced.

- 2025-11-12: treasury moved to the new Safe.

- November 2025: the Stream Finance collapse wiped out the Plasma deployment.

### Current problems and risks

- No value accrual: the protocol fee is 0% and Fee Flow is paused. Holder revenue over the last 30 days is $0.29. Reintroduction has no stated trigger.

- Shrinking, impaired book:

- Net TVL is $252.7M (2026-11-10), against $1.69B on 2025-10-01 and a $4.21B gross peak on 2025-10-07.

- About $196M of the ~$324M in loans is in vaults at 100% utilization with no cash, such as Plasma, Sonic and Avalanche eUSDt-3. Lenders in these vaults cannot withdraw, and headline "borrowed" and "fees" overstate the economic activity.

- Euler Labs itself describes "markets … accumulating bad debt that no one can resolve" in immutable base-layer markets after Stream and Resolv.

- Concentration: Monad holds 77.5% of net TVL and 72% of healthy borrowing. K3 Capital alone curates $166M of Monad supply. K3's September exit from a $205M Ethereum cluster shows how fast large positions leave. Datum noted that Monad's largest vaults were collateral with no borrowing against it ("collateral warehouse").

- Organizational reset: both co-founders are gone, there were layoffs, and the team was quiet for months, per Labs. In its own words, the app is "slow, buggy, and unreliable" and the new backend and app are still being built. EulerSwap was discontinued. Labs says it has runway, but there are no public financials.

- Governance centralization: fees and market sunsets were executed by a 4-of-8 multisig without a 2026 Snapshot vote. Snapshot participation is very low (8 voters on the last vote). The Foundation controls the Treasury. ADMIN_ROLE over the EUL mint sits with the legacy treasury Safe.

- Supply overhang:

- About 25% of supply (~6.9M EUL) sits in Euler-linked Safes.

- Three unlabeled exchange-like EOAs hold ~20% and are active.

- The 2.718% mint is callable at any time.

- Liquidity is thin, at ~$1M/day.

- Competition: Morpho ($10.85B net TVL, also 0% protocol fee) and Aave V3 ($15.01B) dominate (DefiLlama, 2026-11-10). Euler's differentiator (EVC composability, governed vaults) has not translated into share.

- Reputation and data risk: the V1 exploit legacy, the Stream-era losses borne by users of third-party curated vaults, and inconsistent public fee data (the DefiLlama adapter overstatement and gaps) make headline metrics unreliable.

- What is still going well, and what the bulls believe:

- The smart contracts survived two collateral crises without a protocol exploit, and isolation contained the damage.

- Monad grew from ~$3M (2026-05-01) to ~$196M net TVL (2026-11-10, DefiLlama).

- The RWA and institutional pipeline is real: Securitize, VanEck fund, Laser Digital/Keyring, Keyring zk-KYC, Unlink.

- The new leadership has been candid about problems, which bulls read as a credible turnaround.

- At a $21.6M market cap, EUL trades at ~1.5% of MORPHO's market cap for a comparable infrastructure thesis. Bulls see this as optionality on a future fee switch.

### What would move the token

| Catalyst | Timing | Bullish if | Bearish if |

| --- | --- | --- | --- |

| Reintroduction of protocol fees and Fee Flow (DAO proposal plus the minimum-fee upgrade announced in April 2026) | No date published | Fees return on healthy, growing books (Monad, RWA) | Indefinite delay. The upgrade is used without fees. |

| 2.718% EUL mint (~739K EUL) | Callable any time since 2026-01-01 | Remains unused, or is formally renounced | Minted and sold or distributed |

| Laser Digital/Keyring fixed-income markets go live | Announced 2026-09-02, no date | Large committed institutional capital | Delays, or small size |

| New backend, SDK and app; EulerEarn redeploy; curator dashboard | "Upcoming weeks" (stated April 2026); status not confirmed | Shipped, with curator inflows | Further slippage |

| Resolution of stuck vaults (Plasma, Sonic, Avalanche, Ethereum) | Ongoing, no plan published | Recovery or write-down with clarity | Further bad-debt recognition, or headline losses |

| Monad book and K3 Capital positioning | Continuous | Borrow demand arrives on Monad collateral | K3 or Valos withdraw, as on Ethereum in September 2026 |

| Treasury EUL movements (0xC7C5, 0x25aa, 0x0e33) | Any time | Explicit lock or burn policy | Transfers to exchanges |

| Listings and liquidity (Korean exchanges) | Ad hoc | New major listings | Exchange delisting or warning designations |

| Chain deprecations from the official app | 2026 (per Labs) | Focus improves unit economics | Users strand assets, more TVL decline |

