As of 2026-11-10

Unless stated otherwise, on-chain values were read by the author on 2026-11-10 at about 15:18 UTC, at Ethereum block 26,385,357, through https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com. The other chains used their public RPCs: BNB, Sei, Arbitrum and Mantle publicnode/official endpoints, Solana mainnet-beta, Stellar Horizon and XRPL clio. "DL" means DefiLlama and "CG" means CoinGecko. Ondo's own website figures were fetched on the same day. Figures marked Estimate are the author's calculations, not reported numbers. Research limitation: the web-search quota for this run ran out partway through. Later facts were taken from primary pages fetched directly: ondo.finance, docs.ondo.finance, docs.ondoperps.xyz, the Flux governance forum, Tally and Etherscan. A few dated news items from the last 90 days rely on secondary outlets and are labelled that way.

### Executive summary

ONDO is a fixed-supply (10,000,000,000) ERC-20 governance token of the Ondo DAO, which governs Flux Finance. It is economically separate from Ondo Finance Inc., the US company that runs the business. That business is the largest tokenized-treasury and tokenized-stock issuer: USDY at $2.39B, OUSG at $317M, and Ondo Stocks at $1.43B TVL with 470+ assets. It also runs a new equity-perps venue, Ondo Perps, with $79.0M open interest and $376M of rolling 24h volume (Ondo Perps API, 2026-11-10 16:10 UTC). No value reaches ONDO holders today. The token has no fee switch, buyback, burn, staking yield or required utility. DL records $0 holder revenue. The last on-chain DAO proposal was created on 2024-01-12 (FIP-08, token unlock). The only "fee switch" is an anonymous community temperature check from June 2026 that has had no team response. Product revenue goes to Ondo's operating companies and their equity holders. Current state: the products are growing (Ondo Stocks went from "$500M+" TVL on 2026-02-03 to $1.43B; USDY is at about $2.4B). The token, however, is down 46.2% over 1 year and 82.9% from its ATH (CG, 2026-11-10 16:04 UTC). Holders face a corporate-control lawsuit after founder and CEO Nathan Allman died on 2026-05-25, plus continuing treasury distributions: 825M ONDO left the main Ondo multisig in 2026 year to date. The single most important thing to watch is whether the 2027-01-17/18 tranche (1,710.1M ONDO per the DefiLlama unlock dataset) is accompanied by any official value-accrual mechanism. Watch the Delaware control case alongside it, because it currently blocks major corporate changes.

### What the token is

- Ticker / name: ONDO; on-chain name() returns "Ondo" (eth_call 0x06fdde03, 2026-11-10); explorers/Ethplorer display "Ondo Finance". Governance token of the Ondo DAO and of Flux Finance, according to [Ondo Foundation docs](https://docs.ondo.foundation/ondo-token).

- Chain and contract: Ethereum only, 0xfAbA6f8e4a5E8Ab82F62fe7C39859FA577269BE3. Etherscan's verified contract name is "Ondo". CG lists Ethereum as the only platform. The Ondo LayerZero bridge supports USDY and Ondo Stocks, not ONDO ([docs](https://docs.ondo.finance/tools/ondo-bridge)).

- Issuer: Ondo Foundation, a Cayman Islands foundation company, "nonprofit with no beneficial owners". It issues governance tokens, manages the treasury and hosts web apps ([docs](https://docs.ondo.foundation/)).

- History: 10B ONDO were minted on 2022-04-28 to "Ondo Finance: Multisig 2" (Etherscan label). The tokens were non-transferable until 2024-01-18, when DAO Proposal 10 (FIP-08) lifted the lock-up.

