### Revenue and value capture

Bottom line: the products generate real economic flow. Most of it is pass-through yield to product holders. Ondo's own take comes from spreads and fees that are not disclosed. $0 reaches ONDO holders.

#### (a) Gross fees paid by or to users (DL "Ondo Yield Assets": yield paid to USDY+OUSG holders)

| Period | DL dailyFees (pass-through yield) |

| --- | --- |

| 24h (DL total24h, last full day 2026-11-09 UTC) | $306,349 (the in-progress 2026-11-10 data point read $306,398) |

| 7d | $1,757,411 |

| 30d | $7,778,178 (annualized about $94.6M) |

| 1y | $65,814,500 |

| All-time | $96,622,358 |

DL methodology: "the daily yield earned by USDY and OUSG holders … Revenue: Zero. Ondo passes all of this yield to token holders and currently charges no fee." This is not Ondo revenue. Cross-check (Estimate): $2.38B USDY at 3.75% plus $0.317B OUSG at 3.76% gives about $101M a year, or about $8.3M per 30 days. That is consistent with DL's $7.78M per 30 days given USDY growth during the window and daily lumpiness in DL's per-chain data.

#### (b) Protocol and company revenue (goes to Ondo operating companies, not to the DAO)

| Source | Mechanism | Size |

| --- | --- | --- |

| USDY spread | Underlying portfolio yield minus the APY the issuer sets for holders. The issuer, Ondo Global Markets (BVI), keeps the difference. | Estimate: 3.94% YTM − 3.75% APY = 0.19pp. On the $1.97B outstanding reported by Ondo that is about $3.7M/yr. The $0.45B excess of underlying assets over outstanding USDY is not shown to be issuer capital: Ondo's footnote says the 156.90% ratio "excludes US Treasury securities used for structured financing" (Opt-Out Lender Underlyings under Ondo USDY LLC's Tokenized Credit and Security Agreement), so it cannot be treated as free yield to Ondo. Ondo's take is not disclosed. DL records $0. |

| OUSG management fee | 0.15% of AUM | $0 now (waived to 2027-01-01). About $0.48M/yr at current AUM after the waiver ends (Estimate). |

| Ondo Stocks | Quote spread and fees on mint/redeem, retained by the issuer | Not disclosed. Illustration: every 10 bps retained on DL's trailing-1y volume of $9.19B equals about $9.2M/yr. The 30-day pace ($514M) implies about $6.3M/yr per 10 bps. |

| Ondo Perps | Maker/taker fees in USDC, credited to the venue's "Exchange Fee Account (exchange revenue)" per the fee docs. The current 50%-off promotion is 0.01%/0.025% on 77 of 88 markets and 0.015%/0.035% on 11 (live API, 2026-11-10). From 2026-11-13 14:00 UTC the base tier is 0.02%/0.05% (Spot 0.02%/0.06%), with tiers down to −0.005%/0.022%; Ondo Global Markets Spot is 0% until then; Private Markets 0.25%/0.50%. Builders may add up to 10 bps for themselves. | Estimate: on $376M of 24h volume at promotional rates, about $38k/day if all maker and $94k/day if all taker, or about $14–34M annualized before referral discounts and rebates. Launch campaigns may inflate volume (DL notes incentives). Not disclosed. DL's perps volume endpoint is paywalled. |

| Intelligent Portfolios | Annual service fee in the token NAV plus constituent mint/redeem fees | Rates shown per product. AUM not disclosed. Likely small (launched 2026-09-24). |

| Flux Finance | Borrower interest (Compound fork) | $1.64M/1y of interest. DL revenue $0, all to lenders. |

