- 2026-10-05 Ondo Private Markets launched, starting with a pre-IPO AI company ([blog](https://ondo.finance/blog/introducing-ondo-private-markets)).

- 2026-09-28/29 MOU with Kakaopay Securities on distributing Korean equities, signed in Pangyo on 09-28, announced 09-29 ([blog](https://ondo.finance/blog/ondo-and-kakaopay-securities-partner)). ONDO hits its 90-day high of $0.588 on 09-28.

- 2026-09-25 CoinDesk reports that Ondo was shopped to buyers after Allman's death. Ondo calls this "wholly untrue" ([Blockonomi](https://blockonomi.com/ondo-finance-rejects-sale-talk-report-as-court-fight-over-control-continues)).

- 2026-09-24 Ondo Intelligent Portfolios, with three BlackRock-designed strategies ([blog](https://ondo.finance/blog/introducing-ondo-intelligent-portfolios)).

- 2026-09-23 150M ONDO moved from Multisig 2 to distributor 0xea57… (on-chain). Earlier tranches: 08-21 (150M) and 06-22 (150M).

- 2026-09-21/22 In-kind share conversion through Alpaca ITN. Ondo Stocks live on near.com and NEAR Intents.

- 2026-08-06/07 CoinDesk reports the estate's lawsuit, Kathleen C. Allman v. Ondo Finance Inc. (Del. Ch., filed 2026-07-24, before Chancellor Kathaleen McCormick; case number not verified) ([CoinDesk](https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/08/06/power-struggle-erupts-at-ondo-finance-after-founder-s-death), [Parameter](https://parameter.io/ondo-finance-embroiled-in-corporate-control-dispute-following-founders-passing/)).

- August 2026 Ondo Perps expands tokenized-stock collateral to NVDAon, GOOGLon, TSLAon, SNDKon, SPCXon, CRCLon, SLVon and GLDon ([changelog](https://docs.ondoperps.xyz/changelog.md)).

- Context just before the window: 2026-07-27 Ondo Network replaces the "Ondo Chain" L1 plan. About 2026-07-20 Ondo Perps "launched" (public beta listed on DL from 2026-06-09). 2026-07-02 first US-perimeter tokenized securities (IVV, MU) with Broadridge.

- No hacks, depegs or regulatory actions against Ondo products were found in the sources reviewed for this window.

### Current problems and risks

- Governance and control crisis at the company. The founder and controlling shareholder died intestate. His estate (mother, 77, and father, 82) is suing to install a new board and remove Acting CEO De Bode. A court order freezes "major changes". A separate Hawaii petition by his half-sister Dr. Lani Clinton and Ondo investor David Chen seeks to limit Kathleen Allman's control. Any token-economics decision by the company in effect waits on this case. The estate also holds an undisclosed ONDO position.

- Token–business disconnect. Products are scaling (TVL up, BlackRock, DTCC and Fidelity tie-ins), but ONDO captures $0. Governance has been dormant for about 34 months (last proposal 2024-01-12), and the community forum shows frustration (threads from 2026-03-08 and 2026-06-18). Revenue sits in regulated entities with equity owners, so legal barriers to sharing it with token holders are real.

- Supply overhang. 51.8% of supply sits in one multisig with no enforcing vesting contract. Ondo distributed 825M in 2026 and 1.45B in 2025. 1,710.1M more is scheduled for 2027-01-17/18 (DefiLlama), with one or two further equal tranches after that.

- Price trend. −27.7% over 30 days, −46.2% over 1 year and −82.9% from ATH (CG, 2026-11-10 16:04 UTC), while Ondo Stocks TVL roughly tripled from "$500M+" on 2026-02-03 to $1.43B. Ondo Stocks mint/redeem volume, however, fell from $1.39B in March 2026 to $0.47B in October 2026 (DL).

- Revenue opacity. Ondo discloses neither company revenue nor Perps fee revenue. DL reports $0 protocol revenue because the spreads are off-chain. OUSG fees are waived. USDY's spread is thin at about 0.19pp.

- Data inconsistency on USDY. On-chain supply is worth $2.38B, but Ondo's report shows "outstanding" of $1.97B. The headline 156.90% collateralization cannot be reproduced from Ondo's own $2.42B / $1.97B (= 122.9%) and excludes Treasuries used in a structured-financing arrangement (footnote 5 on ondo.finance/usdy).

- Competition. In treasuries, Circle USYC ($2.10B) and BlackRock BUIDL ($1.66B) are close to USDY. In tokenized stocks, Backed/Kraken xStocks, Bitget bStocks, Robinhood's own stock tokens and Dinari compete (Dinari also pledged Anthropic tokens on IPO day). In equity perps, Ondo Perps ($79.0M OI, beta with a $1M position cap) competes with Hyperliquid builder markets and centralized exchanges.

- Centralization and trust. Ondo Perps execution runs in a single enclave. Attestors are permissioned. Product tokens rely on KYC allowlists (OUSG), BVI note issuers and US custodians. US persons are excluded from USDY, Ondo Stocks and Perps.

- Rates. USDY and OUSG yields (3.75–3.76%) follow short-term US rates. If rates fall, the absolute dollar spread shrinks.

What the market believes in: Ondo is the category leader in onchain stocks (about 45–48% share on Ondo's own TVL figure; about 34% on CG category data) and the largest yieldcoin issuer, with unusually strong TradFi integration: BlackRock, DTCC, Fidelity, Broadridge, J.P. Morgan Kinexys and a former House Financial Services Committee Chair as Vice Chairman. The token is bought as the liquid proxy for "tokenization of everything" and as an option on a future fee switch.

